UPDATE companies SET description='1939 Sheet Metal Products, LLC has operated in Cheyenne, Wyoming since its founding in 1939, making it the longest-running HVAC company in the area. What began as a sheet metal and heating operation has continued for over eight decades as a small, owner-operated team serving Southeast Wyoming.

The company provides residential and light commercial HVAC services — including furnace and air conditioning installation, repair, replacement, maintenance, and inspections — alongside in-house custom sheet metal fabrication. Its shop produces ductwork, vents, and specialty metal components, allowing tighter control over fit and turnaround. Additional offerings cover indoor air quality systems, mini-split installation, water heater service, air duct work, and home performance testing.

Customers range from Cheyenne homeowners needing emergency furnace repair during winter cold snaps to small businesses and property managers requiring dependable heating and cooling for daily operations. The firm''s commercial work focuses on practical solutions for light commercial spaces, while residential projects address whole-home comfort, system upgrades, and air quality improvements.

The company emphasizes a quality-first philosophy captured in the maxim that "the bitterness of poor quality remains long after the sweetness of cheap price is forgotten." Its differentiators include owner-involved service — customers often work directly with an owner — fast scheduling often within a week, and fabrication capabilities built for Wyoming''s extreme seasonal swings.', certifications=ARRAY['VETERAN-OWNED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["HVAC installation", "HVAC repair", "HVAC maintenance", "HVAC inspections", "Furnace repair and replacement", "Air conditioning installation and repair", "Sheet metal fabrication", "Custom ductwork fabrication", "Indoor air quality solutions", "Mini-split installation", "Residential HVAC service", "Commercial HVAC service", "Water heater services", "Air duct services", "Home performance testing"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "HVAC"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Often within a week for scheduling", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house sheet metal fabrication shop for custom ductwork and components", "Owner-involved service with direct access to principals", "Fast scheduling, often within a week", "Veteran-owned heritage dating to 1939", "Systems designed for Wyoming climate extremes"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1939 in Cheyenne, WY -> /about", "Veteran-owned -> db, /", "Current owners: Richard Clark, Tanner Weinberger, Ryan Ingersoll -> /about", "Longest-operating HVAC company in Cheyenne -> /, /about", "Small, owner-operated team -> /, /about", "In-house sheet metal fabrication shop -> /, /about, /services", "Services: residential HVAC, commercial HVAC, furnace, AC, indoor air quality, mini-splits, maintenance, inspections, water heater, air duct, home performance testing -> /services", "Custom ductwork, vents, specialty metal components -> /, /services", "Owner-involved service -> /about, /services", "Fast scheduling, sometimes within a week -> /services", "Built for Wyoming conditions -> /, /about", "Class A license number  -> /, /about, /services", "Headquarters at 1019 West 22nd Street, Cheyenne, WY 82001 -> /, /about, /services", "Serves Southeast Wyoming -> /, /services", "Quality-first philosophy quote -> /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='1939-sheet-metal-products-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='1X Technologies is headquartered in Sheridan, Wyoming, and was founded in 2015 as a limited liability company registered in the state. The company''s first commercial order, placed on May 15, 2015, was for robotics products, marking the start of its focus on wire, cable, and electrical equipment for advanced automation.

The company operates as a global distributor and manufacturer of electrical wire, cable, and equipment. Its custom capabilities include cutting, stripping, terminating, marking, shielding, overmolding, connectorization, wire harness assembly, braiding, armoring, mil-spec cable production, private-label packaging, and custom color coding. It also manufactures high-flex robotics cables, copper coils for motors and actuators, and integrated robotics systems such as quadruped robots, robotic arms, humanoid robots, and AGI-integrated platforms, alongside consumer electronics like smart speakers. The firm reports millions of feet of copper and aluminum conductors delivered annually and maintains distribution centers in California, Connecticut, Florida, Illinois, Texas, and Wyoming.

1X Technologies serves a broad range of industries, including aerospace and defense, fusion energy and advanced nuclear, medical equipment, telecommunications, robotics and automation, cybersecurity hardware, wearable technology, consumer electronics, automotive, semiconductor manufacturing, and space exploration. Its customer base includes the U.S. Army Corps of Engineers, U.S. Navy, NASA, and corporations such as Disney, Meta, Google, Apple, Tesla, and ABB.

The company emphasizes its slogan "Because You Require Quality, Quickly!" as a differentiator, citing the industry''s fastest lead times, lowest minimum order quantities, and a dedicated manufacturer sales representative assigned to each account. Products undergo third-party testing by NRTLs including UL, CSA, and ETL, and the firm holds an Essential Critical Infrastructure designation from the Department of Homeland Security, ensuring continuous operation during emergencies.', certifications=ARRAY['UL Listed','MIL-SPEC','CSA','ETL']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wire and cable manufacturing", "Cable cutting, stripping, terminating, marking", "Custom shielding and overmolding", "Connectorization", "Wire harness assembly", "Braiding and armoring", "Mil-spec cable production", "Private label packaging", "Custom color coding", "High-flex robotics cable manufacturing", "Copper coil winding for motors and actuators", "Custom wiring harnesses for industrial and consumer applications", "Integrated robotics systems assembly", "Smart consumer electronics assembly", "Energy-efficient equipment manufacturing"], "industries": ["3D Printing & Additive Manufacturing", "Aerospace & Defense", "Advanced Materials Manufacturing", "Appliance & White Goods", "Artificial Intelligence & Machine Learning", "Automotive", "Biotechnology & Pharmaceuticals", "Broadcast & Communications", "Construction & Building Management", "Consumer Electronics", "Cranes, Hoists & Lifts", "Cybersecurity Hardware Production", "Data Centers & IT Infrastructure", "Education & Research", "Electric Grid Modernization", "Elder Care & Assisted Living", "Emergency Response & Public Safety", "Entertainment & Stage Lighting", "Food & Beverage Processing", "Fusion Energy & Advanced Nuclear", "Government & Public Sector", "Heating & Refrigeration Equipment", "Hospitality & Food Service", "Industrial Automation", "Internet of Things (IoT) Device Manufacturing", "Logistics & Warehousing", "Manufacturing", "