UPDATE companies SET description='3D Plastics Inc. operates from Newberg, Oregon, where it was founded in 2007 as a family-owned plastic injection molding company. The business draws on more than 75 years of combined team experience in project development, product design, and cost-effective manufacturing.

The company runs injection molding machines ranging from 18 to 310 tons, producing parts from one ounce up to 26 ounces (approximately 2 pounds). Capabilities include over-molding with threaded inserts, bushings, and metal or plastic substrates, plus in-house secondary operations such as ultrasonic welding, heat staking, pad printing, hot stamping, CNC machining, and 3D-printed prototypes. Tooling support spans prototype molds (under 500 cycles) to high-production tools exceeding one million cycles.

3D Plastics serves consumer, dental, medical, electrical, and industrial markets. Consumer work includes firework holders, magnifying lenses, and enclosures. Dental components cover caps, holders, handles, and light bezels. Medical projects involve gaskets, DNA holders, and housings. Electrical customers require tight-tolerance housings, electronic packaging, and complex components. Industrial parts are designed for stiffness under extreme pressure and heat. Long-term clients include IceAlert (since 2007) and FEC Source LLC for clear acrylic optical components.

The company positions itself as a single-source partner from concept to final delivery, emphasizing personalized service, full material traceability as a UL-certified molder, and a culture that prioritizes employees, suppliers, and customers alike.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','UL Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "Over-molding (insert molding)", "Pad printing", "Hot stamping", "Ultrasonic welding", "Ultrasonic inserting", "Milling", "Drilling", "Tapping", "Sub-assembly", "Final assembly", "Component sourcing", "Painting", "Adhesive bonding", "Vacuum metalizing", "CNC machining", "3D printed prototypes", "Tooling design and fabrication", "Design assistance", "Material selection assistance"], "industries": ["Consumer", "Dental", "Medical", "Electrical", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Elastomers", "Structural foam", "Filled thermoplastics", "Stainless steel", "Brass", "Anodized aluminum", "Clear acrylic", "Silicone", "Thermoplastics"], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines (18\u2013310 ton capacity)"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production (500 to 1,000,000+ cycles)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["UL-certified molding with full material traceability", "Single-source supplier from concept to finished product", "In-house secondary operations including pad printing, ultrasonic welding, and CNC machining", "Mold tooling support for prototype to high-volume production", "Family-owned operation with over 75 years of combined team experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2007 -> db", "41 employees -> db", "Headquarters Newberg, Oregon -> db", "ISO 9001 certified -> db", "Family-owned -> /", "75+ years combined team experience -> /", "Injection molding machines 18-310 tons -> /services", "Parts 1 ounce to 26 ounces -> /services", "8,360,346 parts molded in 2025 -> /", "76 customers -> /", "Over-molding with inserts, bushings, contacts, plastic substrates -> /services", "In-house sonic welding, heat staking, post-mold machining -> /services", "Value-added services: pad printing, hot stamping, ultrasonic welding, ultrasonic inserting, milling, drilling, tapping, sub assembly, final assembly, component sourcing, painting, adhesive bonding, vacuum metalizing, CNC, 3D printed prototypes -> /services", "Tooling support with mold classifications (prototype to 1,000,000+ cycles) -> /services", "Industries served: consumer, dental, medical, electrical, industrial -> /services", "Consumer examples: firework holders, magnifying lenses, enclosures -> /services", "Dental examples: caps, holders, handles, bezels for lights -> /services", "Medical examples: gaskets, DNA holders, housings -> /services", "Electrical examples: housings, electronic packaging, complex components -> /services", "Industrial examples: stiff products, parts up to 2 pounds -> /services", "IceAlert partnership since 2007 -> /", "FEC Source LLC clear acrylic optical components -> /", "UL certified molder with total traceability -> /services", "Single-source supplier from concept to final product -> /services", "Materials: elastomers, structural foam, filled materials, stainless steel, brass, anodized aluminum, softer plastic over rigid plastic -> /services", "Design assistance and material selection -> /services"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='3d-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='425 Fabrication Division operates from a 45,000-square-foot facility in Rockford, Illinois. The division was formed in 2012 as part of 425 Manufacturing, which Mike and Michelle Thomason founded to provide general machining services and aftermarket parts for drilling equipment in the greater Rockford area. As community building projects brought steady fabrication work, the Thomasons established the Fabrication Division as a dedicated unit. The company remains family-owned and employee-driven, with the Thomason family active in local charitable giving.

The shop combines metal fabrication, welding, and precision machining under one roof. In-house welding includes MIG, TIG, stick, and arc gouging on stainless steel and aluminum, supported by a mobile welding rig for on-site repairs. Machining capacity comprises four CNC turning centers, four CNC machining centers, multiple knee and bed mills, manual lathes, and three surface grinders. A 3-ton overhead crane and two heated paint booths (one 12''×14''×30'', another 14''×24''×14'') handle large weldments. The division also runs a 3D printing lab for rapid prototyping and production parts, a CMM-equipped inspection room, and augmented-reality tools for design verification.

Customers span industrial heat-treat equipment builders, custom machine builders, drilling and mining, wind power, air and water filtration, food processing, paper machinery, power generation, aerospace maintenance, marine maintenance, semi-truck upfitters, retail fixture makers, and automotive suppliers. The division has developed a nationwide niche in aircraft static display mounting, delivering custom-machined components and precision-fit assemblies for museums and military bases. Emergency mobile welding has served fire departments and other fleets needing rapid, on-site repairs.

The Thomasons started the business to fill a local machining gap, and the fabrication division grew from demand for engineered structural solutions. The company emphasizes AWS-certified welding personnel, in-house engineering and 3D design, and a culture of community involvement—evidenced by donations such as 2,300 pounds of pet food to a local shelter.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AWS Certified']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["MIG Welding", "TIG Welding", "Stick Welding (Mobile/Off-site)", "Arc Gouging", "Stainless Steel Welding", "Aluminum Welding", "Plasma Cutting", "Sand Blasting", "Industrial Painting & Coatings", "CNC Milling", "CNC Turning", "Surface Grinding", "Vertical & Horizontal Sawing", "3D CAD & Engineering", "Solid Modeling", "3D Printing / Rapid Prototyping", "Honing", "Waterjet Cutting (outsourced)", "Wire EDM (outsourced)", "Conventional EDM (outsourced)", "Coating/Plating: Oxide, Anodize, Chrome (outsourced)", "Heat Treating (outsourced)", "Gear Broaching/Hobbing (outsourced)", "Laser Cutting (outsourced)", "Static Display Mounting (Aircraft)", "Mobile Welding Services", "3D Design and Rendering", "CMM Inspection", "Augmented Reality for Sizing"], "industries": ["Aerospace Maintenance", "Marine Maintenance", "Drilling & Mining", "Wind Power", "Air/Water Filtration & Treatment", "Food Processing", "Paper Machinery", "Power Generation", "Industrial Heat Treat Equipment", "Custom Machine Building", "Semi-Trucks", "Retail", "Automotive", "Aircraft Static Display", "Fire/Emergency Vehicles"], "materials": ["Stainless Steel", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["CNC Turning Centers (4)", "CNC Machining Centers (4)", "CNC Knee Mills (2)", "CNC Bed Mill (1)", "Manual Knee Mill (1)", "Manual Lathes (2)", "Surface Grinders (3)", "Honing Machine", "Sandblasting Equipment", "3-ton Overhead Crane", "Heated Paint Booth (12''\u00d714''\u00d730'')", "Heated Paint Booth (14''\u00d724''\u00d714'')", "CMM", "3D Printers", "Augmented Reality System"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned, employee-driven culture with community focus", "AWS-certified welding staff and ISO 9001:2015 quality system", "45,000 sq ft facility with 3-ton crane and dual heated paint booths", "In-house 3D printing lab for rapid prototyping and additive production", "Mobile welding rig for on-site emergency repairs"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2012 -> db", "Founders Mike and Michelle Thomason -> /about", "Family-owned, employee-driven -> / (testimonials), /about", "45,000 sq ft facility in Rockford, IL -> /", "3-ton crane, heated paint booths (12''x14''x30'' and 14''x24''x14'') -> /, /services", "AWS-Certified, ISO 9001:2015 -> /", "In-house welding: MIG, TIG, Stick, Arc Gouging, Stainless, Aluminum -> /services", "Mobile welding rig -> /about, /services", "Machining: 4 CNC turning centers, 4 CNC machining centers, 2 CNC knee mills, 1 CNC bed mill, 1 manual knee mill, 2 manual lathes, 3 surface grinders, honing -> /services", "3D printing lab for rapid prototyping and production -> /services", "CMM inspection, augmented reality -> /services", "Industries served list -> /", "Additional industries: aerospace, semi-trucks, retail, automotive -> /about", "Aircraft static display mounting nationwide -> /services", "Emergency mobile welding for fire department -> / (testimonial)", "Community donation 2,300 lbs pet food -> /about", "Staff: Mike Thomason (President), Tyler Thomason (Fabrication Manager, AWS cert, first responder), Dena Aldridge, Mike Lemery, Wyatt Beaird -> /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='425-fabrication-division-and-mobile-welding' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='ADCO Plastics Corporation, based in Marietta, Georgia, has been producing custom injection molded assemblies and parts since its founding in 1974.

The company runs 22 injection molding machines with clamping forces from 55 to 750 tons, capable of molding parts weighing 2 to 64 ounces. Its process portfolio includes insert molding, sonic welding, heat staking, pad printing, hot stamping, painting, and secondary machining such as cutting, drilling, and CNC milling. ADCO also provides full and sub-assembly, in-house mold building, product design and development, and PPAP documentation, supported by statistical process control and Six Sigma tools.

ADCO serves the medical, commercial, industrial, transportation, and retail markets, working with commodity resins, engineered resins, and thermoplastic rubbers.

The company emphasizes agile customer responsiveness, fast quoting and lead times, and value-added design and manufacturing as its core differentiators. Its quality management system is certified to ISO 9001:2015.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding (55-750 ton)", "Insert molding", "Sonic welding", "Heat staking", "Pad printing", "Hot stamping", "Painting", "CNC machining (cutting, drilling, milling)", "Assembly (full and sub-assembly)", "Mold building", "Product design and development", "Production Part Approval Process (PPAP)", "Axis mechanical probing", "Statistical process control (SPC) / Six Sigma", "Quality management system (ISO 9001:2015)"], "industries": ["Medical", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Transportation", "Retail"], "materials": ["Commodity resins", "Engineered resins", "Thermoplastic rubbers"], "equipment": ["22 injection molding machines (55-750 ton)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Agile customer responsiveness and problem solving", "Fast estimates, quotes, and lead times", "Value-added design and manufacturing", "In-house mold building capability", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1974 -> db", "Headquartered in Marietta, Georgia -> db", "22 injection molding machines ranging from 55 to 750 tons -> /", "Part weight range 2 to 64 oz -> db, /", "Insert molding, sonic welding, heat staking -> db", "Pad printing, hot stamping, painting -> db", "Secondary services: cutting, drilling, CNC milling -> db", "Assembly (full & sub-assembly) -> db", "Mold building -> /", "Industries served: medical, commercial, industrial, transportation, retail -> db", "Materials: commodity grade and engineered resins and thermoplastics rubbers -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> db, /", "Value-added design and manufacturing -> /", "Agile customer responsiveness -> /", "Fast estimates, quotes, lead times -> /", "Product design and development -> db", "PPAP -> db", "Axis mechanical probing -> db", "Six Sigma tools, SPC, control charts, capability studies -> db"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='adco-international-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='AIM Processing was founded in 1993 in Longmont, Colorado, by a toolmaker and a plastics processor who started with two presses. The company initially handled overflow and complex projects for other molders, building a reputation for difficult small-part work. In 2006, the founders retired and sold the business to the current management team.

Today, AIM operates 37 injection molding presses around the clock in a nearly 60,000-square-foot facility that includes a 40,000-square-foot production plant and an 18,000-square-foot finished-goods warehouse. The company specializes in custom plastic injection molding of small parts—defined as between the size of a fingernail and a hand—using a mix of automated lights-out production and press-side attended operations. Services include insert molding, overmolding, metal replacement, tooling and tool transfer, and secondary operations such as laser etching, ultrasonic welding, and assembly. Engineering support focuses on design for manufacturability. The firm has launched nearly 2,000 distinct small plastic parts for over 100 customers.

AIM serves manufacturers in agriculture, automotive, industrial manufacturing, electronics, medical, and safety and security sectors. Typical clients are manufacturers with 30–300 employees who need engineering support for new programs; many have been customers for a decade or more. Testimonials cite a medical device company president and an industrial product company quality manager.

The company emphasizes three attributes: determination, appetite for innovation and creativity, and focus on customer value through quality. It maintains ISO 9001:2015 registration, reports a 98%+ on-time delivery rate, and uses forecasting models so that over 85% of custom parts ship from stock. Its central Colorado location enables two-day ground shipping to 16 states.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Small-part plastic injection molding", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Metal-to-plastic conversion", "Tooling design and management", "Tool transfer", "Laser etching and part marking", "Ultrasonic welding", "Assembly", "Design for manufacturability (DFM) engineering support"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Automotive", "Industrial Manufacturing", "Electronics", "Medical", "Safety and Security"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 registered quality system", "98%+ on-time delivery rate", "Over 85% of custom parts ship from stock via forecasting models", "Two-day ground shipping to 16 states from central Colorado facility", "24/7 automated and attended production on 37 presses"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1993 in Longmont, Colorado by a toolmaker and plastics processor -> /about-us", "Founders retired and sold to present management in 2006 -> /about-us", "37 presses running 24/7 -> /, /about-us, /services", "Facility expansions: 1998 (16,000 sqft), 2014 (40,000 sqft), 2021 (warehouse to 18k sqft, total nearly 60k sqft) -> /about-us", "Specializes in small plastic parts (fingernail to hand size) -> /, /about-us, /services", "Services: injection molding, insert molding, overmolding, metal replacement, tooling, tool transfer, secondary services (laser etching, ultrasonic welding, assembly), engineering support -> /, /services", "Launched nearly 2,000 parts for over 100 customers -> /about-us, /services", "Industries served: Agriculture, Automotive, Industrial Manufacturing, Electronics, Medical, Safety and Security -> /, /about-us, /services", "Typical clients: manufacturers with 30-300 employees, 10+ year relationships -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 registered -> /, /about-us, /quality", "98%+ on-time delivery rate -> /, /about-us", "85% of custom parts ship from stock via forecasting -> /", "Two-day ground shipping to 16 states from Longmont, CO -> /", "Automated lights-out production and press-side attended operations -> /services", "Testimonials from medical device company president and industrial product company quality manager -> /, /about-us"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='aim-processing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Acadiana Textiles & Supply was founded in 1997 in Lafayette, Louisiana. The company is a woman-owned and veteran-owned wholesale distributor that has served businesses across the Gulf Coast region and beyond for over two decades. The company operates from its Lafayette headquarters and ships throughout the Gulf Coast and beyond.

As a wholesale-only distributor, the company supplies industrial wiping rags, oil absorbents, spill kits, packaging supplies such as stretch wrap, and disposable protective garments. Its product catalog includes specific lines such as 30120 polypropylene protective apparel, CGS428 Chem-Guard protective apparel, FGF127 Flash-GuardFR flame-resistant protective apparel, and DSP303 DanGuard protective apparel.

The customer base consists of approved business accounts including distributors, industrial suppliers, marine suppliers, janitorial suppliers, safety suppliers, and automotive parts stores. All purchases require account approval and a valid resale certificate, and the company does not sell to the general public or end users.

Acadiana Textiles & Supply states that its focus is on dependable service, flexible packaging options, competitive wholesale pricing, and building long-term customer relationships. The wholesale-only model is designed to support resellers and industrial supply chains rather than direct consumer sales.', certifications=ARRAY['Woman Owned']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale distribution of industrial wiping rags", "Wholesale distribution of oil absorbents", "Wholesale distribution of spill kits", "Wholesale distribution of packaging supplies", "Wholesale distribution of disposable protective garments", "Flexible packaging options for wholesale orders", "Account management for approved business customers"], "industries": ["Industrial suppliers", "Marine suppliers", "Janitorial suppliers", "Safety suppliers", "Automotive parts stores", "Distributors"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Wholesale-only distribution with mandatory account approval", "Woman-owned and veteran-owned business", "Flexible packaging options for resellers", "Competitive wholesale pricing", "Focus on long-term customer relationships"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1997 -> db", "Headquartered in Lafayette, Louisiana -> db", "Woman-owned and veteran-owned -> db", "Wholesale distributor of wiping rags, oil absorbents, spill kits, packaging supplies, disposable protective garments -> /", "Serves distributors, industrial suppliers, marine suppliers, janitorial suppliers, safety suppliers, automotive parts stores -> /", "Wholesale-only, requires resale certificate -> /", "Focus on dependable service, flexible packaging, competitive pricing, long-term relationships -> /", "Product lines: 30120 Polypropylene, CGS428 Chem-Guard, FGF127 Flash-GuardFR, DSP303 DanGuard -> /", "Certification: Woman Owned -> db"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='acadiana-textiles-supply' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Accumedix, Inc. was founded in 2001 and operates from Libertyville, Illinois. The privately held company is led by President Paul J. Serio, a medical device industry veteran with over 35 years of experience at Baxter Healthcare and Fenwal Blood Technologies, and Vice President of Regulatory Affairs and Quality Michele H. Kupcso, who brings similar depth from Baxter and Allegiance Healthcare. Serio joined after global IT acquisitions and SAP implementations, while Kupcso previously ran an international regulatory consulting firm.

The company provides end-to-end medical device commercialization services, spanning design and development, quality management system implementation, contract manufacturing, assembly and packaging, and distribution. Its Libertyville facility includes clean room and white room manufacturing environments capable of handling clinical trial runs through full production scale. Services include sterile packaging, sterilization coordination (including ethylene oxide requalification and quarterly dose audits), lot-controlled warehousing, and drop-shipping. Accumedix also offers a subscription-based quality management system that covers FDA and European management representation, annual registrations, audits, and supplier quality oversight.

Its client engagements cover catheter assembly, electromechanical device assembly, and broader device commercialization programs that require regulatory submissions such as 510(k)s, European technical files, and FDA quality system compliance.

The company''s stated mission is to develop and commercialize new medical device technologies while generating returns for investors through outstanding customer value.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485','ISO 9001','ISO MDSAP','Medical Device Directive','FDA 21 CFR Part 820','SOR/98-282','UL']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design for manufacturability", "Design control", "Project management", "510(k) submission support", "Regulatory facility registration", "Device master record maintenance", "Device history record maintenance", "Quality system consulting", "Sterile packaging", "Sterilization coordination", "Sterilization validation", "Warehousing with lot control", "Clean room manufacturing", "White room manufacturing", "Clinical trial manufacturing", "Full-scale production manufacturing", "Lot control and serialization", "In-process quality assurance", "Final quality assurance", "MRP material tracking", "Finished goods warehousing", "Distribution and drop-shipping", "Quality system subscription management", "Catheter assembly", "Electromechanical assembly"], "industries": ["Medical Devices"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Clinical trial to full production scale", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 2001 -> db, /about", "Headquarters Libertyville, Illinois -> db, /about", "FDA registered facility -> /about", "Certifications: ISO MDSAP, ISO 13485, ISO 9001, Medical Device Directive, FDA 21 CFR Part 820, SOR/98-282, UL -> /about, /quality", "President Paul J. Serio, 35 years experience at Baxter/Fenwal -> /about", "VP Michele H. Kupcso, 35 years experience at Baxter/Allegiance -> /about", "Services: design/development, quality management, assembly/packaging, contract manufacturing, distribution -> /services", "Clean room and white room manufacturing -> /services", "Clinical trial through full production scale -> /services", "Customers: individual inventors to Fortune 1000 -> /", "Assembly and packaging any q