UPDATE companies SET description='All American Woodworks operates from Emigrant, Montana, just outside Yellowstone National Park. The company was founded in 1996 by Steve Sirois, a third-generation New England craftsman who served with the 82nd Airborne in Iraq and Afghanistan, earning a Bronze Star for building housing and shower facilities for soldiers. After his military service, Sirois met his future wife Christine, began contracting in Nevada, and relocated the business to Montana in 2007. The shop is veteran-owned and family-operated, with Christine co-managing operations.

The shop specializes in custom CNC carving, furniture making, cabinetry, mantles, built-in bookcases, media wall cabinets, pet beds, and custom EcoPoxy epoxy creations. It also serves as an authorized retailer for EcoPoxy resins and a dealer for CabinetParts.com hardware. All pieces are designed and fabricated in-house, from initial consultation through final finish, and can be shipped anywhere in the continental United States. No facility size or headcount figures are published.

Customers range from residential homeowners seeking one-of-a-kind furniture, live-edge tables, and decorative carvings to commercial clients needing custom built-ins, office libraries, and branded fixtures. The company also serves military and patriotic markets with challenge-coin cases, badges, and memorial pieces, and supplies pet products such as hardwood kennels and beds. EcoPoxy products are sold to DIYers, artists, and professionals nationwide.

Sirois founded the business on principles of loyalty, trust, honesty, and integrity, emphasizing guaranteed one-of-a-kind craftsmanship and customer satisfaction. The shop''s veteran ownership, third-generation woodworking heritage, and partnership with the "Made in Montana" program are cited as key differentiators, along with its authorized status for EcoPoxy and CabinetParts.com.', certifications=ARRAY['Veteran Owned']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom CNC carving", "Furniture making", "Cabinetry", "Mantles", "Repairs", "Pet beds", "Media wall cabinets", "Home office and library built-ins", "Built-in bookcases and shelves", "Custom EcoPoxy creations", "EcoPoxy retail sales", "CabinetParts.com dealer services"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Military", "Pet Products", "Furniture", "Cabinetry", "Woodworking", "Retail"], "materials": ["Domestic woods", "Exotic imported woods", "EcoPoxy epoxy resins", "Black walnut", "Birdseye maple", "Hardwoods"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Veteran-owned and operated", "Family-owned with third-generation craftsmanship", "Authorized EcoPoxy retailer", "Authorized CabinetParts.com dealer", "Custom CNC carving and in-house design-to-finish service", "Ships anywhere in the continental U.S.", "Made in Montana partner"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1996 -> db", "Headquarters in Emigrant, Montana -> db", "Veteran-owned certification -> db", "Founder Steve Sirois, third-generation craftsman -> /about-us", "Steve Sirois served in 82nd Airborne, Iraq and Afghanistan, Bronze Star -> /about-us", "Family-owned, Christine co-manages -> /about-us", "Relocated to Montana in 2007 -> /about-us", "Custom CNC carving, furniture, cabinetry, mantles, built-ins, pet beds, EcoPoxy creations -> /", "Authorized EcoPoxy retailer -> /", "Authorized CabinetParts.com dealer -> /", "Ships anywhere in continental US -> /", "Principles of loyalty, trust, honesty, integrity -> /", "30+ years experience -> /", "Made in Montana partner -> /about-us", "Materials: domestic and exotic woods, EcoPoxy epoxy resins, Black walnut, Birdseye maple, hardwoods -> /", "Serves residential, commercial, military/patriotic, pet products, retail -> /, /about-us"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='all-american-woodworks-cst' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Alliance Wire & Cable was established in 1998 in Lawrenceville, Georgia, when Sergio Marti and Mike Strong combined their experience in wire and cable distribution to serve the metro Atlanta area.

The company operates as a distributor of wire and cable products, maintaining an extensive inventory that includes fiber and copper assemblies, pre-terminated cables, connectivity products, raceway and wiring duct solutions, and a range of specialty cables such as fire alarm, security, coaxial, category, fiber optic, medium voltage, solar PV, and tray cables. From its Georgia facility and a second location opened near Dallas, Texas in July 2016, Alliance serves customers across the United States, the Caribbean, and Mexico.

Its customer base spans electrical, datacom, and specialty contractors in the Southeast, as well as commercial, industrial, and residential sectors. Specific industries served include energy management, renewable energy (wind and solar), and industrial automation. The company supplies products for applications ranging from building wire and access control to variable frequency drive cables and motor lead wire.

Alliance differentiates itself through a focus on customer service, which the founders credit for early growth and expansion. Partnerships with manufacturers enable competitive pricing on quality products, while the dual-location model allows broader inventory availability and faster fulfillment. The company states it is committed to maintaining high service levels while adapting to evolving market conditions and technology.', certifications=ARRAY['MIL-SPEC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fiber and copper cable assembly", "Pre-terminated cable assembly", "Connectivity product supply", "Raceway and wiring duct supply", "Wire and cable distribution", "Inventory management and fulfillment"], "industries": ["Electrical contractors", "Datacom contractors", "Specialty contractors", "Energy management", "Renewable energy", "Wind energy", "Solar energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Extensive inventory across two U.S. locations (Georgia and Texas)", "Customer service focus since founding", "Partnerships with manufacturers for quality products at competitive prices", "Serves Southeast, Caribbean, Mexico, and broader U.S."], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1998 by Sergio Marti and Mike Strong -> /about", "Headquartered in Lawrenceville, Georgia -> db", "Second location opened near Dallas, TX in July 2016 -> /about", "Serves electrical, datacom, and specialty contractors in Southeast -> /", "Extensive inventory serving US, Caribbean, Mexico -> /", "Industries served: Energy Management, Renewable Energy, Wind Energy Cables -> db", "Certification: MIL-SPEC -> db", "Products include fiber & copper assemblies, pre-terminated assemblies, connectivity products, raceway and wiring duct solutions -> /", "Capabilities: services from Georgia facility -> db", "Commitment to customer service and partnerships with manufacturers -> /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='alliance-wire-cable' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Microsemiconductor, Inc. was incorporated in 1972 in Madison, New Jersey. The company began as a supplier of semiconductors and discrete active electronic components to major industrial accounts worldwide.

The firm operates as both a manufacturer and distributor of electronic components, specializing in diodes, thyristors, transistors, and optoelectronics. It maintains an inventory of over 500,000 items and offers access to more than 2,000,000 electronic parts, including obsolete and hard-to-find integrated circuits such as IGBTs and MOSFETs. The staff consists primarily of sales and logistics professionals who manage a supply chain monitored for reliability and risk. The company reports that 95 percent of deliveries ship overnight with no line-item minimum.

Customers span commercial, industrial, medical, military, and aerospace sectors. The company serves major industrial accounts globally, providing components for high-reliability applications and supporting the repair and life extension of existing electronic systems.

American Microsemiconductor emphasizes personal customer relationships, promising to know each client by name and understand their business needs. Its quality assurance program is registered to AS9100D and ISO 9001:2015, aiming to exceed expectations for product quality, delivery, authentication, and price. The company also highlights its communication channels—phone, fax, email, online chat, and Skype—as part of its service model.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Semiconductor distribution", "Obsolete component sourcing", "Integrated circuit replacement and repair", "Quality assurance (AS9100D, ISO 9001:2015)", "Supply chain management", "Sales and logistics support"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Industrial", "Medical", "Military", "Aerospace"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "95% of deliveries overnight", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["2,000,000+ electronic parts available", "500,000+ inventoried items", "95% of deliveries overnight", "No line item minimum", "Specialist in obsolete and hard-to-find semiconductors"], "facts_used": ["Incorporated in 1972 -> /about", "Headquarters in Madison, New Jersey -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 and AS9100D certifications -> /quality", "2,000,000+ electronic parts available -> /", "500,000+ inventoried items -> /", "95% of deliveries overnight -> /", "No line item minimum -> /", "Specializes in diodes, thyristors, transistors, optoelectronics -> /", "Serves commercial, industrial, military, aerospace, medical industries -> /about, /quality", "Obsolete component sourcing and replacement -> /about", "Staffed by sales and logistics professionals -> /about", "Supply chain monitoring and risk filtering -> /about", "Communication via phone, fax, email, chat, Skype -> /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "la