UPDATE companies SET description='American Pasteurization Company (APC) was founded in 2004 in Wauwatosa, Wisconsin. The company began as the first provider of High Pressure Processing (HPP) on a commercial tolling basis to the food and beverage industry, offering a pay-as-you-go model that lowered the barrier for manufacturers to adopt the technology.

APC operates as a contract processor and co-manufacturer, delivering HPP services alongside post-process packaging, pack-off, and assembly. The company also provides product development guidance from concept through commercialization and refers customers for refrigerated transportation. Specific facility size, headcount, and annual throughput are not disclosed.

The company serves food and beverage manufacturers across categories including ready-to-eat meats, plant-based proteins, fresh poultry and pork, sausage, seafood, egg-based products, dairy, beverages such as wheatgrass juice and energy drinks, and avocado-based items like guacamole. Customers range from emerging brands to established producers seeking extended shelf life and food safety without thermal pasteurization.

APC differentiates itself through its pioneering tolling model, which allows clients to access HPP without capital investment in equipment. The firm emphasizes its SQF certification and its role in guiding clients through packaging selection and regulatory considerations for HPP-treated products.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["High Pressure Processing (HPP)", "Toll processing (pay-as-you-go)", "Co-manufacturing", "Post-HPP packaging", "Pack-off services", "Assembly services", "Refrigerated transportation referrals", "Product development consulting", "Packaging selection guidance", "Regulatory compliance support"], "industries": ["Food and beverage manufacturing", "Meat and poultry processing", "Plant-based protein", "Seafood processing", "Dairy processing", "Beverage production", "Ready-to-eat foods", "Avocado and dip products"], "materials": ["Ready-to-eat meat products", "Plant-based protein products", "Fresh poultry and pork", "Sausage products", "Seafood products", "Egg-based products", "Dairy products", "Beverage products", "Avocado-based products"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First commercial HPP tolling provider in the U.S.", "Pay-as-you-go processing with no equipment capital expenditure", "Co-manufacturing and post-HPP packaging under one roof", "SQF-certified facilities", "Product development support from concept to commercialization"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2004 -> db", "Headquarters in Wauwatosa, Wisconsin -> db", "First company to offer HPP on commercial tolling basis -> db", "Provides HPP on pay-as-you-go basis -> db", "Offers co-manufacturing of premium food products -> db", "Offers post-HPP packaging, pack-off and assembly services -> db", "Provides refrigerated transportation service referrals -> db", "SQF certified -> db", "Serves food and beverage industry -> db", "Product categories: ready-to-eat meats, plant-based proteins, fresh poultry, sausage, seafood, egg-based, dairy, beverages, avocado-based -> db", "Industries served: wheatgrass, energy drinks, nutritional supplements -> db"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='american-pasteurization-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Arcadia Manufacturing Group was founded in 1969 by James T. Sumner in Green Island, New York. Sumner began the business from his living room and the trunk of his car, supplying drills, taps, and saw blades. In 1979 his son William Sumner joined the company, and together they expanded it into a premium metals service center offering specialty metals, cutting tools, and precision cutting services. Today the company operates as a registered veteran-owned small business with two facilities totaling 88,000 square feet.

The group provides full-service, in-house contract manufacturing of fabricated metal parts, components, and assemblies. Its capabilities span waterjet cutting (multi-head tables up to 144 by 286 inches), laser cutting (Trumpf fiber lasers up to 1-inch thick carbon steel), CNC machining (4-axis vertical and horizontal centers holding ±0.0005-inch tolerances), certified welding (GMAW, GTAW, stud and plasma processes), fabrication (rolling, bending, punching, drilling, saw cutting), and assembly (sub-components, full assemblies, kitting). Design engineering and project management support round out the turnkey offering.

Arcadia serves customers across the transportation, architectural, infrastructure, energy, medical, military, defense, and construction industries throughout the United States.

The company traces its differentiation to the founding principles of superior customer service, a passion for metals, and a willingness to tackle difficult challenges. Its veteran-owned status and full-service, under-one-roof model are presented as key advantages for clients seeking a single-source partner.', certifications=ARRAY['AWS','DOT','DIN','Veteran Owned Small Business']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Waterjet cutting", "Laser cutting", "CNC machining (4-axis)", "CNC forming", "Press brake forming", "Welding (GMAW, GTAW, stud welding, plasma cutting)", "Fabrication (rolling, bending, punching, drilling, saw cutting)", "Assembly (sub-components, full assemblies, kitting)", "Design engineering", "Inspection (FARO arm, Virtek laser QC)", "Turnkey manufacturing", "Engineering support and project management", "Sub-vendor coordination (painting, galvanizing, powder coating)"], "industries": ["Transportation", "Architectural", "Infrastructure", "Energy", "Medical", "Military", "Defense", "Construction"], "materials": ["Carbon steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Brass", "Copper", "Various metals"], "equipment": ["Trumpf 2030 2KW fiber laser", "Trumpf 1040 6KW fiber laser", "Haas VF-7/50 Vertical Machining Center", "Haas VF-6/50 Vertical Machining Center", "Haas VF-10/50 Vertical Machining Center", "Samsung PCV 400 Vertical Machining Center", "Makino a81 Horizontal Machining Center", "Waterjet 48\" x 144\" single-head table", "Waterjet 96\" x 200\" 2-head table", "Waterjet 144\" x 240\" 2-head table", "Waterjet 144\" x 286\" 2-head table", "Waterjet 100\" x 203\" 2-head table", "Trumpf V2300S Press Brake", "Trumpf TruBend 5320 Press Brake", "Tri-Acro Pacific Hydro/Mechanical press brake", "Marvel Series 81 saw", "Grizzly G0614 miter saw", "Lincoln 265 Power Mig welders", "Lincoln Powerwave 445 welders", "Miller XMT 350 welders", "Miller Dynasty 280/400 TIG welders", "Miller Syncrowave 250 DX TIG welders", "Miller Deltaweld 350", "Nelson NCD 1600 Stud Welder", "Hypertherm Max 200 Plasma Cutter", "FARO Platinum Arm", "Virtek Laser QC System", "Starrett Granite Inspection Table"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.0005 in", "built_on": ["Veteran-owned small business", "Full-service in-house contract manufacturing from design to delivery", "Two facilities totaling 88,000 sq ft", "Multi-head waterjet cutting up to 8\" thick", "CNC machining tolerances of \u00b10.0005 inch"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1969 by James T. Sumner -> /about", "Started in living room and car trunk -> /about", "William Sumner joined 1979 -> /about", "Veteran-owned small business -> /about, /", "Headquarters Green Island, NY -> /about", "Two facilities totaling 88,000 sq ft -> /about, /capabilities", "Industries served: transportation, architectural, infrastructure, energy, medical, military, defense, construction -> /about", "Capabilities: waterjet, laser, CNC machining, welding, fabrication, assembly, design engineering -> /services, /capabilities", "Equipment: Trumpf lasers, Haas mills, Makino, waterjet tables, press brakes, welding machines, inspection equipment -> /capabilities", "Tolerances \u00b10.0005 inch -> /capabilities", "Certifications: AWS, DOT, DIN -> /capabilities", "Materials: carbon steel, stainless steel, aluminum, brass, copper -> /capabilities"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='arcadia-mfg-group' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The original founder, Ben Gosey, started with a single used bag machine, selling by day and producing by night, and later expanded into printing and extrusion operations in Fort Smith before consolidating in Van Buren.

Today APP operates as a vertically integrated custom flexible packaging manufacturer on a 10‑acre campus with 68,000 square feet of production space and a 5,000‑square‑foot office. The company extrudes its own film — offering LDPE, LLDPE, MDO, multi‑layer, PCR, biodegradable and compostable grades — prints up to 10 colors on flexographic presses equipped with AVT scan and ColorCert technology, and converts the printed web into bags, pouches, liners, sleeves and wicketed products through slitting, rewinding, folding, laminating, zip‑lock and gusseting. Additional in‑house services include graphic design, plate making, inventory management, warehousing and a private fleet for shipping.

APP serves the poultry industry — its original market — as well as broader food and beverage processors that require SQF and Global Food Safe certified packaging. Its customer base spans regional, national and international accounts seeking custom poly bags, films, liners and retail merchandise bags.

The company emphasizes vertical integration as its core differentiator, citing control over scheduling, shorter lead times and the ability to recycle 100 % of ink, scrap film and corrugated material. Quality systems include a HACCP‑based process, internal testing, and a reported product return rate below 1 %.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF','Global Food Safe Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Extrusion (LDPE, LLDPE, MDO, Multi-Layer, PCR, Biodegradable, Compostable)", "Flexographic printing (up to 10 colors)", "Specialized inks", "Computerized color matching", "Color registration", "Graphics design", "Slitting", "Rewinding", "Folding", "Lamination", "Pouch making", "Zip lock", "Gusseting", "Wicketing", "Print plate development", "Total inventory control", "Warehousing", "Shipping services", "Internal testing capabilities"], "industries": ["Poultry", "Food and beverage"], "materials": ["LDPE", "LLDPE", "MDO", "Multi-Layer", "PCR", "Biodegradable", "Compostable"], "equipment": ["AVT Scan Technology", "ColorCert Technology"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated extrusion, printing and converting under one roof", "Up to 10\u2011color flexographic printing with AVT scan and ColorCert process control", "SQF and Global Food Safe certified with HACCP\u2011based quality system", "Less than 1\u202f% product return rate", "Private fleet and on\u2011site warehousing for controlled shipping"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2001 by partners Sarah Sparks Diebold and R. Trent Goins -> db, /about", "Origins trace to early 1970s with Ben Gosey -> /about", "Facility: 10 acres, 68,000 sq ft manufacturing, 5,000 sq ft office -> /capabilities", "Processes: extrusion, flexographic printing up to 10 colors, converting -> /capabilities", "Materials: LDPE, LLDPE, MDO, Multi-Layer, PCR, Biodegradable, Compostable -> /capabilities", "Certifications: SQF, Global Food Safe Certification -> /about", "Quality: HACCP-based process, AVT Scan, ColorCert, <1% return rate -> /about", "Industries: poultry, food and beverage -> /about, /", "Sustainability: 100% recycling of ink, scrap film, corrugated -> /about", "Private fleet for shipping -> /capabilities", "Location: Van Buren, Arkansas, near I-40/I-49, rail and river access -> /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='arkansas-poly-printing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Atsumi Car Equipment Inc. operates its North American manufacturing facility in Wytheville, Virginia. The company was established in 2001 as the U.S. subsidiary of Atsumi Kogyo Co., Ltd., a Japanese precision machining firm founded in 1950 in Hamamatsu, Japan.

The facility specializes in precision machining of automotive components, including hubs, spindles, starter shafts, and engine variable valve timing (VVT) rotors. Production processes encompass precision grinding, sintered metal machining, heat treatment, and forged metal machining, supported by automated NC lathes, drilling machines, and a multiple-articulation transfer robot. Automated machining lines incorporate in-process inspection with autocheckers, auto gauges, and auto alarming systems. The Wytheville site is part of a global network that includes factories in Japan, Indonesia, Thailand, and Mexico.

Atsumi Car Equipment serves the automotive industry, supplying Tier 1 manufacturers such as NSK (for Toyota, Lexus, and Honda hubs and spindles), Aisin (for Nissan and GM VVT rotors), and Denso (for Toyota starter tubes). The company''s customer base spans OEMs and major automotive suppliers across North America and globally through its affiliated plants.

The company emphasizes its automated, inspection-integrated machining lines and a quality structure built on QC and TPM activities, which it says enable consistent high-quality output across both small and large production volumes. Its U.S. facility is staffed by American workers dedicated to American customers, leveraging the parent company''s decades of automotive machining experience.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision grinding", "Sintered metal machining", "Heat treatment", "Forged metal machining", "Hub machining", "Spindle machining", "Starter shaft machining", "Engine variable valve timing (VVT) rotor machining", "Automated NC lathe machining", "Drilling", "Multiple-articulation transfer robot automation", "Automated machining with in-process inspection (autocheckers, auto gauges, auto alarming)", "Four-wheel axle production", "Shaft precision machining", "Sintering"], "industries": ["Automotive"], "materials": ["Sintered metal", "Forged metal"], "equipment": ["Automated NC lathes", "Drilling machines", "Multiple-articulation transfer robot", "Automated machining lines with in-built autocheckers, auto gauges, auto alarming systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Automated machining lines with in-process inspection (autocheckers, auto gauges, auto alarming)", "Global manufacturing network with facilities in Japan, Indonesia, Thailand, U.S., and Mexico", "Specialization in hub, spindle, starter shaft, and VVT rotor precision machining", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "QC and TPM activities supporting both low- and high-volume production"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Wytheville, VA -> /", "Parent company Atsumi Kogyo Co., Ltd. founded 1950 in Hamamatsu, Japan -> /", "U.S. subsidiary Atsumi Car Equipment Inc. founded 2001 -> /about-us", "Ownership: led by Kakuzo Atsumi (Chairman) and Setsuzo Atsumi (President) -> /about-us", "Specializes in hub, spindle, starter shaft, VVT rotor precision machining -> /", "Processes: precision grinding, sintered metal machining, heat treatment, forged metal machining -> /", "Automated NC lathes, drilling machines, multiple-articulation transfer robot -> /about-us", "Automated machining lines with autocheckers, auto gauges, auto alarming -> /", "Global network factories in Japan, Indonesia, Thailand, U.S., Mexico -> /about-us", "Customers: NSK (Toyota, Lexus, Honda), Aisin (Nissan, GM), Denso (Toyota) -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certification attained 2018 -> /about-us", "Materials: sintered metal, forged metal -> /", "QC and TPM activities for quality structure -> /about-us", "American workers for American customers -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='atsumi-car-equipment-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Available Plastics, Inc. was founded in 1978 in Huntsville, Alabama. The company operates as a woman-owned small business specializing in PVC manufacturing.

The company produces custom plastic pipe, tube, and related products for manufacturers, wholesalers, and distributors across North America. Its core processes include injection molding, custom plastic fabrication and assembly, custom extrusion, and additional cleaning for medical and cleanroom applications. Available Plastics also offers custom coloring services driven by volume requirements, and manufactures proprietary product lines such as the Banner Hanging System and FlowMax Gold central vacuum tubing. The product portfolio includes custom extrusion profiles, furniture-grade PVC pipe and fittings, and industry-standard PVC pipes and tubes.

Available Plastics serves a range of industries including film and textile winding, utilities, water filtration, petroleum, sporting goods, construction, outdoor furniture and home furnishings, and retail display. Its customer base consists of manufacturers, wholesalers, and distributors throughout North America.

The company emphasizes on-time delivery of quality PVC products and utilizes the latest manufacturing technologies with premium-grade PVC materials to produce what it describes as superior PVC products. Its woman-owned status and focus on medical-grade cleaning capabilities further distinguish its offering.', certifications=ARRAY['WOMAN OWNED']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection Molding", "Custom Plastic Fabrication & Assembly", "Custom Extrusion", "Medical/Cleanroom Cleaning", "Custom Coloring (Volume Driven)", "Banner Hanging System Manufacturing", "FlowMax Gold Central Vacuum Tubing Manufacturing"], "industries": ["Film and Textile Winding", "Utilities", "Water Filtration", "Petroleum", "Sporting Goods", "Construction", "Outdoor Furniture and Home Furnishings", "Retail Display"], "materials": ["PVC", "Premium-grade PVC"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Woman-owned small business", "On-time delivery of quality PVC products", "Latest manufacturing technologies with premium-grade PVC", "Medical and cleanroom cleaning capabilities", "Custom coloring driven by volume"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1978 -> db, /", "Headquarters in Huntsville, Alabama -> db", "Woman-owned small business -> db, /", "Manufactures custom plastic pipe, tube, and products -> /", "Processes: injection molding, custom plastic fabrication & assembly, custom extrusion, medical/cleanroom cleaning, custom colors -> /", "Industries served: film and textile winding, utilities, water filtration, petroleum, sporting goods, construction, outdoor furniture and home furnishings, retail display -> /", "Customer types: manufacturers, wholesalers, distributors throughout North America -> /", "Uses premium-grade PVC materials -> /", "Offers Banner Hanging System and FlowMax Gold central vacuum tubing -> /", "Certification: Woman Owned -> db"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count"