' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bergen Cable Technology was founded in 1942 in Lodi, New Jersey, and today operates from Fairfield, New Jersey. The company began as an innovator in wire rope and cable assembly, and claims to be the longest continuously operating manufacturer in that field.

The company produces a range of cable-based products including safety cables, control cables, lanyards, push-pull controls, custom cable assemblies, LockClad cables (per MIL-DTL-87218), miniature cables, and termination bands qualified to M85049/128-3 and -4. Manufacturing processes include rotary swaging for tight tolerances, cutting and stripping with Ewald flash cutters, crimping using hydraulic and pneumatic presses up to 175 tons, pull testing up to 22,500 lbf with full-length validation to 106 feet, finishing via electromechanical etching, hot stamping, metal stamping, heat-shrink markers, and laser marking, and packaging that can meet military specifications.

Bergen serves aerospace, military and defense, spacecraft, robotics, medical, emerging technology, transportation, marine, electronics, power generation, and commercial aviation. It is an approved supplier for numerous aerospace and medical companies and has received multiple Boeing Performance Excellence Awards, including Gold in 2010 and Silver in several other years.

The company emphasizes its 80-plus-year legacy, unmatched technical expertise, and customer service as differentiators. It holds multiple U.S. Government QPL certifications, AS9100D and ISO 9001:2015 registrations, and ITAR certification, and states that its mission is to continue innovating while protecting the entrepreneurial spirit that started the business.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100D','ISO 9001:2015','ITAR','M85049/128-3','M85049/128-4','U.S. Government QPL certifications']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Rotary swaging", "Cutting and stripping (Ewald flash cutters)", "Crimping (hydraulic and pneumatic presses up to 175-ton)", "Pull testing (proof and destructive up to 22,500 lbf, full-length validation up to 106 ft)", "Finishing (electromechanical etching, hot stamping, metal stamping, heat shrink markers, laser marking)", "Packaging (including military-specification packaging)", "Custom cable assembly design and manufacturing", "Safety cable manufacturing", "LockClad cable assemblies (MIL-DTL-87218)", "Control cables (push-pull and pull-pull configurations)", "Lanyard assembly", "Miniature cable assembly", "Termination bands (qualified to M85049/128-3 and M85049/128-4)", "Precision machining"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Military and defense", "Spacecraft", "Robotics", "Medical", "Emerging technology", "Transportation", "Marine", "Electronics", "Power generation", "Commercial aviation"], "materials": ["Wire rope", "Cable", "Aircraft cable (MIL-DTL-87218)", "Steel bands", "Coated cable"], "equipment": ["Ewald flash cutters", "Hydraulic presses (up to 175-ton)", "Pneumatic presses", "United testers", "Customized digital proof loaders", "Purpose-built pull test facility (22,500 lbf, 106 ft)", "Rotary swaging machines", "Laser marking equipment", "Hot stamping equipment", "Electromechanical etching equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Longest continuously operating wire rope and cable assembly manufacturer (since 