ridge-industries' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Bon Foods traces its roots to 1947 when Paul Le Vasseur Bonneau founded the company in Portland, Oregon, as a manufacturer and contract packager of food‑grade gravy, soup and sauce bases. The business expanded into vapor‑distilled water and logistics in 1975, added a food‑business incubator and additional facilities in 2014, and became a subsidiary of Icon Foods, Inc. in 2018. Today it operates two manufacturing plants and two distribution centers in the Portland area, encompassing more than 80,000 square feet of processing and warehouse space.

The company provides turnkey co‑packing and co‑manufacturing for liquid and dry products, ranging from gram‑size packages to full rail‑car loads. Core capabilities include hot‑fill and cold‑fill co‑packing, custom dry and liquid blending, particle milling and grinding (down to 0.1 micron), contract beverage manufacturing, toll processing, and analytical quality services. An on‑site R&D team supports formula development, gluten‑free and all‑natural projects, and clean‑label innovation, while an incubation program helps emerging brands scale without large capital outlays.

Bon Foods serves the food and supplement industries, with a customer base that includes chain restaurants, supermarkets, and brands lacking in‑house hot‑fill or cold‑fill equipment. Recent projects have covered sauces, condiments, dips, dressings, soup bases, gravy bases, marinades, specialty sugars, vinegars and syrups.

The company emphasizes its 70‑year track record, third‑party‑audited GMP facilities, HACCP plans on every line, kosher certification through the Oregon Kosher Rabbinical Council, and a full suite of packaging options — lug and continuous‑thread caps, mylar and induction sealing, tamper‑evident banding, glass and plastic containers — to deliver consistency and food safety from concept to commercial viability.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2008','GMP','HACCP','Kosher Certification (Oregon Kosher Rabbinical Council)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hot fill co-packing", "Cold fill co-packing", "Custom dry blending", "Custom liquid blending", "Custom milling and grinding", "Contract beverage manufacturing", "Contract manufacturing and packaging", "Toll processing for food", "Quality reprocessing services", "Analytical and quality services", "Bulk handling", "Dry processing", "Liquid processing", "Research and development", "Gluten-free formula development", "All-natural formula development", "Kosher co-packing", "Incubation services"], "industries": ["Food and supplement industries", "Chain restaurants", "Supermarkets"], "materials": ["Beverages", "Sweeteners", "Sauces", "Dips", "Dressings", "Gravy bases", "Soup bases", "Flavors", "Specialty sugar products", "Vinegars", "Syrups"], "equipment": ["Media particle grinding and milling equipment (0.1 micron capability)"], "volume": "Gram-size packages to full rail car loads", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["70 years of quality food experience (since 1947)", "Hot-fill and cold-fill co-packing at every facility", "On-site R&D teams for formula development (gluten-free, all-natural, clean label)", "Kosher-certified and third-party audited GMP facilities with HACCP on every line", "Incubation program to launch brands without major capital investment"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1947 by Paul Le Vasseur Bonneau -> /about", "Acquired by Icon Foods, Inc. in 2018 -> /about", "Operates two manufacturing facilities and two distribution centers in Portland, Oregon area with over 80,000 sq ft -> /about", "Co-packer and co-manufacturer of liquid and dry products for food and supplement industries, from gram-size to rail car loads -> /about", "Offers hot fill and cold fill co-packing services -> /services", "Custom dry & liquid blending, custom milling and grinding, contract beverage manufacturing -> /services", "ISO 9001:2008 certified facility with media particle grinding and milling equipment capable of 0.1 micron -> /services", "GMP, HACCP, food safety and food defense trained staff, Kosher Certification with Oregon Kosher Rabbinical Council -> /services", "R&D support for formula development, gluten-free, all-natural, clean label -> /", "Incubation program for food businesses -> /", "Packaging options: lug and continuous thread caps, mylar or induction sealing, tamper evident banding, glass and plastic containers -> /", "Serves chain restaurants, supermarkets, clients without hot fill/cold fill equipment -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='bon-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Brevan Electronics is headquartered in Nashua, New Hampshire. The company was formed in 1983 as a distributor of high-technology electronic components for original equipment manufacturers. It is a woman-owned business led by CEO Michelle Dufoe.

Today Brevan operates as a global distributor and value-added service provider. Its core offerings include authorized distribution of passives, interconnects, and electromechanical components, along with custom cable assemblies, wire harnesses, and PCB assembly. The company also provides supply chain services such as bill-of-materials management, global sourcing, vendor-managed inventory, excess inventory liquidation, and shortage solutions. Through its subsidiaries Micro Informatica (serving Latin America and the Caribbean since 1985, acquired in 2025) and Falcon Electronics (specializing in aerospace and defense semiconductors, acquired in 2024), Brevan extends its reach into harsh-environment markets.

The customer base spans original equipment manufacturers across the electronics industry, with a noted focus on aerospace and defense programs through Falcon Electronics. Brevan’s authorized distribution lines cover top component manufacturers, and its proprietary cloud-based sourcing platform grants access to billions of parts worldwide.

Brevan differentiates itself through its woman-owned status and a culture that emphasizes employee growth and professional development under Dufoe’s leadership. The company promotes a “BRVN Guarantee” of highest-quality service, backed by 24/7 real-time quoting from dedicated account specialists and a proprietary sourcing technology that enables rapid response to component shortages.', certifications=ARRAY['UL Listed']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assembly", "Wire harness assembly", "Electronic sub-assembly", "PCB assembly", "Bill of Materials (BOM) management", "Global sourcing", "Excess inventory management", "Vendor Managed Inventory (VMI)", "Shortage solutions / component sourcing", "Authorized distribution of electronic components", "Passives distribution", "Interconnects distribution", "Electromechanical components distribution", "Real-time quoting", "Supply chain solutions"], "industries": ["Aerospace and defense", "Original equipment manufacturers (OEMs)", "Electronics industry"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Woman-owned business with leadership focused on employee development", "24/7 real-time quoting via dedicated account specialists", "Excess inventory management program offering free valuations and flexible options", "Proprietary cloud-based sourcing technology accessing billions of electronic parts globally", "Vendor Managed Inventory (VMI) services for stock-level forecasting and warehouse operations"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Nashua, New Hampshire -> db", "Founded in 1983 -> /about-us", "Woman-owned business -> /about-us", "CEO Michelle Dufoe -> /about-us", "Started as distributor of high-technology electronic components for OEMs -> /about-us", "Offers custom cable assemblies, wire harnesses, PCB assembly -> /about-us, /", "Provides BOM management, global sourcing, VMI, excess inventory management, shortage solutions -> /services", "Subsidiary Micro Informatica (Latin America/Caribbean, since 1985, acquired 2025) -> /", "Subsidiary Falcon Electronics (aerospace/defense semiconductors, acquired 2024) -> /", "Authorized distributor for top electronic component manufacturers -> /services", "Proprietary cloud-based sourcing technology accessing billions of parts -> /services", "24/7 real-time quotes with dedicated account specialist -> /, /services", "BRVN Guarantee: highest quality service and solutions -> /, /about-us", "Recognized as 2025 Top 50 Global Distributor -> /about-us", "Certification: UL Listed -> db"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='brevan-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='BrightLife Electric NV is based in Sparks, Nevada, and was founded in 2020 during the global pandemic. The company is woman-owned and family-operated, started by Shannon, who grew up in Spanish Springs in a family of contractors and spent years learning the electrical trade before launching the business with a vision to build a lasting, integrity-driven operation.

The firm provides a full range of residential and commercial electrical services, from troubleshooting single outlets and panel upgrades to complete rewiring, new-construction wiring, and commercial tenant improvements. The team works on projects of all sizes, offering free estimates and maintaining current licensing, bonding, and insurance (License #0087070).

BrightLife serves homeowners, property managers, and commercial contractors across Reno, Sparks, Spanish Springs, Washoe County, Carson City, and surrounding Northern Nevada communities. Typical customers include residential clients needing repairs or remodels, builders on new housing developments, and businesses requiring tenant improvements, lighting retrofits, or EV charging infrastructure.

The company emphasizes honest, transparent communication and a family-first culture that provides livable wages and benefits to its electricians. Shannon notes that her woman-owned perspective brings a different approach to attention to detail and customer service. This philosophy has earned consistent community recognition, including five consecutive years as a Nextdoor Neighborhood Favorite and multiple Best of Reno awards.', certifications=ARRAY['WOMAN-OWNED','Licensed, bonded, and insured (License #0087070)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential electrical repair and replacement", "Panel upgrades", "Rewiring", "Device and lighting installation", "Troubleshooting and testing", "New construction wiring", "Security lighting installation", "Ceiling fan installation", "Surge protection installation", "RV outlet installation", "EV charger installation", "Inspection and testing", "Dedicated circuits and equipment wiring", "Commercial tenant improvements", "Lighting retrofits", "Commercial remodel and retrofit", "Commercial maintenance and repairs", "Subpanel repairs", "Single breaker replacement", "Free estimates", "Recessed lighting installation", "Transfer switch installation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "New construction", "Tenant improvements", "Commercial remodeling", "EV charging infrastructure"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 2020 during pandemic -> db", "Woman-owned, family-operated -> db, /about-us", "Founder Shannon, background in construction -> /about-us", "Headquarters Sparks, Nevada -> db", "13 employees (13 families) -> /about-us", "Services: residential and commercial electrical, panel upgrades, rewiring, lighting, EV chargers, etc. -> /, /services", "License #0087070, licensed/bonded/insured -> /services", "Service area: Reno, Sparks, Spanish Springs, Northern Nevada -> /, /about-us, /services", "Nextdoor Neighborhood Favorite 2020-2025 -> /", "Best of Reno awards 2023-2025 -> /", "Community Choice Award #1 in Reno & Sparks -> /", "Free estimates -> /services", "Woman-owned perspective on communication -> /about-us", "Family-first culture, livable wages -> /about-us"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='brightlife-electric-nv' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Brookfield Wire, LLC operates from a 40-acre site in West Brookfield, Massachusetts, where it has been drawing and shaping wire since 1947. The company was founded as a domestic manufacturer of cold-drawn stainless steel, nickel, and nickel-alloy wire, and today runs over 70,000 square feet of manufacturing space supported by a 15-acre solar array that helps power the facility.

The core business is precision wire drawing and forming, producing round, flat, and custom-shaped wire in diameters from 0.006 to 0.250 inches. The plant houses electric strand annealing furnaces and draws countless tons of stainless steel, nickel, Inconel, and other alloys each year, offering more than 50 standard alloys plus hard-to-find grades sourced globally from domestic and NATO-qualified mills. Finished wire ships on spools, reels, coils, Acro Pacs, and cut-to-length packages.

Typical applications include spring wire, welding electrode core wire, medical component wire, fine cable sheathing, slickline and downhole line, brush wire, and fastener wire for nails, staples, and screws.

Brookfield Wire emphasizes DFARS-compliant materials, ISO 9001:2015 certification, and quick lead times as key differentiators. The company’s seven-decade track record, extensive alloy inventory, and willingness to source obscure grades are presented as reasons customers choose them over brokers or offshore suppliers.', certifications=ARRAY['DFARS','ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire drawing (fine and ultra-fine)", "Wire forming (shaped, flat, round)", "Custom shaped wire (net-shape cross-sections)", "Flat wire rolling (ribbon wire) with edge conditioning", "Round wire drawing to close tolerances", "Electric strand annealing", "Straightening and cutting", "Die-drawn shapes", "Custom tempering", "Spooling and packaging (coils, reels, Acro Pacs, catchweight coils, cut-to-length)", "Wire drawing for stainless steel, nickel, nickel alloys, Inconel"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Agriculture", "Medical", "Automotive", "Oil and gas", "Building and construction", "Welding", "Jewelry", "Telecommunications", "Animal cage fabrication", "Belting, mesh, and screening", "Fasteners", "Machining", "Cable and hose sheathing", "Shot blasting and abrasives", "Spring manufacturing", "Brush manufacturing", "Marine", "Rope and cable", "Screen and mesh"], "materials": ["300 series stainless steel", "Nickel", "Nickel-based alloys", "Inconel"], "equipment": ["Electric strand annealing furnaces", "State-of-the-art drawing dies", "Rolling mills for flat wire", "Wardwell 16 & 24 Carrier", "Hacoba"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["DFARS-compliant wire materials", "ISO 9001:2015 certified", "Quick lead times on custom and stock wire", "50+ standard alloys in stock with global sourcing for hard-to-find grades", "70+ years of continuous wire manufacturing experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1947 -> db", "Headquarters West Brookfield, Massachusetts -> db", "40-acre site with 15-acre solar field and 70,000 sq ft manufacturing area -> /about-u