UPDATE companies SET description='Bunty LLC is headquartered in Greenville, South Carolina. The company was founded in 2000 by Rajeev Jindal, a Clemson University engineering graduate with corporate manufacturing experience at International Paper, Milliken & Company, and Owens Corning. Jindal started the business as a contract manufacturing firm, which later evolved into a full-service custom machined, forged, and cast metal parts fabrication enterprise. Jeffrey Pham, a Babson College graduate and former consultant to the U.S. Air Force and DaimlerChrysler, serves as Managing Director.

The company provides a broad range of metalworking services, including custom forging (closed-die, cold forging), casting (die, investment, permanent mold, sand, centrifugal, and lost-foam), CNC machining (5-axis, milling, turning, EDM wire cutting), heat treatment, surface treatments (anodizing, plating, powder coating, DLC), and fabrication with tooling. Bunty operates domestic and overseas manufacturing, warehousing, and inspection facilities, supporting production from prototype through full-run volumes. No specific facility size or headcount is disclosed.

Bunty serves the automotive, aerospace, energy, medical, and food-processing industries. Its customer base includes the world’s largest tire manufacturer, a transmission supplier to a major Japanese automaker, Tier I automotive manufacturers of shocks, brakes, drivetrain components, and mirror assemblies, as well as producers of stainless-steel parts for food processing that meet FDA standards.

The company emphasizes a flexible, adaptive business model that combines global sourcing with reduced overhead and agility. It highlights rapid turnaround—offering delivery of stocked parts within one to three days—volume discounts, an extensive inventory of metal shapes, and rigorous process control protocols certified to AS9100D and ISO 9001:2015. Bunty positions itself as a partner that brings global manufacturing capabilities to small and mid-sized businesses.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100D','ISO 9001:2015','CVMSDC']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Closed-die forging", "Cold forging", "Investment casting (lost wax)", "Die casting", "Permanent mold casting", "Sand casting", "Centrifugal casting", "Lost foam casting", "5-axis CNC machining", "CNC milling", "CNC turning", "EDM wire cutting", "Laser cutting", "Plasma cutting", "Honing", "Lapping", "Heat treating (annealing, normalizing, quenching, tempering)", "Case hardening (carburizing, nitriding)", "Anodizing", "Powder coating", "Plating (chrome, nickel, etc.)", "DLC coating", "Metal stamping (progressive die)", "Welding (aluminum, titanium)"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Aerospace", "Energy", "Medical", "Food processing"], "materials": ["Steel", "Gray iron", "Ductile iron", "Malleable iron", "Bronze", "Aluminum alloys", "Brass alloys", "Copper alloys", "Nickel silver alloys", "Stainless steel", "Nickel alloys", "Titanium alloys", "Magnesium alloys", "Carbon fiber", "Magnesium Elektron"], "equipment": ["5-axis CNC machining centers", "CNC milling machines", "EDM wire cutting machines", "Laser cutting systems", "Plasma cutting systems"], "volume": "Prototype to mass production", "lead_time": "1-3 days for stocked parts; rapid turnaround for production orders", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Global manufacturing network with domestic and overseas facilities", "AS9100D and ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system", "Rapid delivery of stocked parts within 1\u20133 days", "Prototype-to-mass-producti