UPDATE companies SET description='C C Mouldings Inc. was founded in 1986 in Albuquerque, New Mexico. The veteran-owned business serves the Greater Albuquerque area, including South Valley, Rio Rancho, and Santa Fe.

The company specializes in custom woodworking and moulding, offering over 150 distinct design profiles for trim, flooring, thresholds, t-molds, reducers, and mantles. It also provides custom millwork and consultation services for both private and commercial projects.

Its customers span residential and commercial construction, as well as DIY enthusiasts seeking wholesale pricing. The firm has built a reputation over decades for supplying moulding and millwork to homeowners and contractors throughout central New Mexico.

C C Mouldings emphasizes wholesale pricing and a full-service approach that combines fabrication with design consultation. The company highlights its A+ Better Business Bureau rating and veteran ownership as markers of reliability.', certifications=ARRAY['Veteran-Owned']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom woodworking", "Moulding fabrication", "Custom millwork", "Consultation services", "Flooring and threshold fabrication", "T-mold and reducer production"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Commercial construction"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Wholesale pricing on all moulding and millwork", "Over 150 standard moulding design profiles", "Custom millwork and design consultation services", "Veteran-owned and operated"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 -> db", "Headquarters Albuquerque, New Mexico -> db", "Veteran-owned -> db", "Services: custom woodworking, moulding, millwork, consultation, flooring, thresholds, t-molds, reducers, mantles -> db", "Over 150 design profiles -> db", "Service area: Greater Albuquerque, South Valley, Rio Rancho, Santa Fe -> db", "A+ BBB rating -> db", "Wholesale pricing -> db"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='c-c-mouldings-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='CM Manufacturing, Inc. was founded in 1986 in Missoula, Montana by Richard Johnson, a retired United States Air Force officer who served as Commander of the Defense Contract Management Agency (DCMA) in Cleveland. After a career that included program management at Cleveland Pneumatic on the SH-60B and EA-6B aircraft programs, Johnson established the company to apply his aerospace expertise to precision machining.

The shop specializes in fracture-critical and flight-safety-critical landing gear components for nearly every aircraft flown by the U.S. military and many foreign air forces. It machines high-strength steels such as 300M, 4340, and 4330; nickel alloys including Inconel, 13-8PH, and 17-4PH; plus aluminum and Delrin. Production runs on rigid Mazak equipment, and the company states it commonly holds tolerances of ±0.0001 inch. Inspection capabilities include multiple coordinate measuring machines (Brown & Sharpe G2000, Mitutoyo Crysta-Plus M574, Global S Green 9.12.8), optical and digital comparators (Starrett HB400 and HDV400-M3-CNC), a VICI vertical vision system, and a full suite of height gages, bore gauges, and thread gages.

Customers span the aerospace and defense sectors, including major aircraft manufacturers and the Defense Logistics Agency. The company emphasizes long-term vendor relationships and a proactive scheduling module to meet delivery commitments.

Johnson founded the business on a legacy of quality, precision, and craftsmanship developed during his military service and subsequent industry roles. That ethos was passed to Ken Johnson during 18 years working alongside his father before Richard''s passing in 2014, and it continues to drive the company''s focus on on-time, on-budget delivery of critical components.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100:2016','ISO 9001:2015','ITAR Registered','Oasis Registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision CNC machining", "Landing gear component manufacturing", "Fracture-critical parts machining", "Flight-safety-critical parts machining", "CMM inspection (Brown & Sharpe, Mitutoyo, Global S)", "Optical comparator inspection (Starrett HB400)", "Digital comparator inspection (Starrett HDV400-M3-CNC)", "Vision measuring system inspection (VICI MTL 500)", "Height gage inspection (Trimos series)", "Bore gauge inspection (Holematic)", "Thread gaging", "Micrometer inspection", "Quality management (AS9100)", "Material processing: high-strength steels, nickel alloys, aluminum, Delrin"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Defense", "Military aircraft"], "materials": ["300M", "Inconel", "13-8PH", "17-4PH", "4340", "4330", "Delrin", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["Mazak CNC machines", "VICI Vertical Vision Measuring System MTL 500 Ergon", "Starrett HB400 Optical Comparator", "Starrett HDV400-M3-CNC-2LED-EXT Horizontal Digital Comparator", "Brown & Sharpe G2000 Coordinate Measuring Machine", "Mitutoyo Crysta-Plus M574 Coordinate Measuring Machine", "Global S Green 9.12.8 Coordinate Measuring Machine", "Trimos V Plus Height Gage", "Trimos V600+ Plus Height Gage", "Trimos V3 & V5 Height Gages", "Trimos V4 Height Gage", "Holematic Digital Bore Gauge", "Thread gages (.086\"-11.2500\")", "Micrometers (0-13\")", "Blade Micrometers (0-6\")", "Pitch Micrometers (0-6\")", "GAGE Pins (.011\"-1.0\")"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.0001 inch", "built_on": ["Commonly holds tolerances to \u00b10.0001 inch", "Specializes in fracture-critical and flight-safety-critical landing gear components", "Proactive scheduling module for on-time delivery", "Long-term established vendor relationships"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 by Richard Johnson -> /about-us", "Richard Johnson retired as Commander of DCMA Cleveland -> /about-us", "Ken Johnson joined 1996, now CEO & Owner -> /about-us", "Headquarters Missoula, Montana -> db", "Specializes in fracture critical and flight safety critical landing gear components -> /", "Materials: 300M, Inconel, 13-8PH, 17-4PH, 4340, 4330, Delrin, Aluminum -> /", "Commonly hold tolerances to \u00b10.0001 -> /", "Mazak machines -> /", "Certifications: AS9100:2016, ISO 9001:2015, ITAR Registered, Oasis Registered -> /", "Inspection equipment list -> /quality", "Customers: U.S. military aircraft, foreign countries, Defense Logistics Agency -> /, /about-us", "Proactive scheduling module, long-term vendor relationships -> /", "Family-owned legacy passed from Richard to Ken Johnson -> /about-us"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='c-m-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1963 in Conyers, Georgia, C+K Plastics by Georgia Thermoforming operates a 95,000-square-foot manufacturing facility east of Atlanta. A second plant in Metuchen, New Jersey mirrors the equipment and capabilities, allowing tooling to move between sites for added capacity and freight savings.

The company specializes in large-format thermoforming, offering vacuum forming, pressure forming, twin-sheet forming, and heavy-gauge vacuum forming for parts up to 16 feet long in gauges from .080 to .780 inch. Its Conyers plant houses advanced equipment including a Zero-Sag machine—the first of its kind in the U.S. for automated large twin-sheet forming—along with CNC trimmers and robotics. Secondary operations such as CNC trimming take projects from concept to finished product, supporting both low- and high-volume runs.

A noted specialty is returnable packaging for automotive manufacturers to transport parts to assembly plants.

C+K Plastics emphasizes technological advancement to deliver innovative, cost-effective thermoforming solutions. The dual-plant network shortens lead times and enables just-in-time and blanket-order fulfillment, while the Zero-Sag machine provides a unique capability for large twin-sheet parts with enclosed cavities suited for structural applications.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Vacuum forming", "Pressure forming", "Twin-sheet forming", "Heavy-gauge vacuum forming", "Secondary operations", "CNC trimming", "Returnable packaging", "Just-in-time delivery", "Blanket orders", "Tooling transfer between facilities", "Concept to finished product support"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Transportation", "Aerospace", "OEM manufacturing"], "materials": ["ABS", "PVC", "Polycarbonate"], "equipment": ["Zero-Sag machine", "CNC trimmers", "Robotics"], "volume": "Low and high-volume parts", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Zero-Sag machine: first U.S. automated large twin-sheet forming system", "Dual-plant network (Conyers, GA and Metuchen, NJ) for shorter lead times and tooling transfer", "95,000 sq ft facility with advanced robotics and CNC trimmers", "Just-in-time and blanket-order fulfillment capability", "Low-cost tooling modifications and fast sample turnaround"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1963 in Conyers, Georgia -> /", "95,000 sq ft facility in Conyers -> /", "Second plant in Metuchen, New Jersey -> /", "Processes: vacuum forming, pressure forming, twin-sheet forming, heavy-gauge vacuum forming -> /", "Parts up to 16 feet long, gauges .080 to .780 inch -> /", "Zero-Sag machine (first in US for automated large twin-sheet forming) -> /", "CNC trimmers and robotics -> /", "Secondary operations, concept to finished product -> /", "Low and high-volume production -> /", "Industries: automotive (returnable packaging), transportation, aerospace, OEM manufacturers -> /", "Returnable packaging for automotive manufacturers -> /", "JIT and blanket orders -> /", "Tooling transfer between plants -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> /", "Materials: ABS, PVC, polycarbonate -> /", "Company emphasizes technological advancement for innovative cost-effective solutions -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='c-k-plasticsthermoforming-georgia' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='CM Fabricating is a veteran-owned metal fabrication shop based in Kansas City, Missouri. The company was established in 2015 as a local fabrication and welding business serving the Kansas City metropolitan area, founded to deliver quality craftsmanship and affordable service to the region.

The shop offers custom metal fabrication, welding (including mobile welding), powder coating, and CNC cutting services. The facility uses CNC cutting equipment for intricate patterns and large-scale projects, while a mobile welding unit allows on-site repairs and installations. No facility size or headcount figures are publicly disclosed.

CM Fabricating works with residential, commercial, and industrial clients across Kansas City and surrounding communities such as Independence, Riverside, Gladstone, and Roeland Park. Past projects cited in customer reviews include custom railings, range hoods, wine shelving units, stair railings, and fabrication for both personal acreage and professional job sites.

The company emphasizes fast turnaround, offering same-day service and free estimates. It is licensed and insured, and provides a 10 percent discount for veterans and first responders. According to the company, its commitment to quality and customer satisfaction sets it apart, backed by licensed and insured operations and a policy of same-day service availability.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Metal Fabrication", "Welding Services", "Mobile Welding Services", "Powder Coating Services", "CNC Cutting Services"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day services; fast turnaround times", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day service availability", "Free estimates on all projects", "10% discount for veterans and first responders", "Licensed and insured operations", "40+ years of combined fabricator and welder experience"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2015 -> db, /about", "Headquarters: Kansas City, MO -> db, /, /about", "Veteran-owned -> db, /, /about", "Services: custom metal fabrication, welding, mobile welding, powder coating, CNC cutting -> /, /about", "40+ years combined experience of fabricators and welders -> /about", "Licensed and insured -> /, /about", "Free estimates -> /, /about", "Same-day services -> /, /about", "10% discount for veterans and first responders -> /, /about", "Service areas: Kansas City, Independence, Riverside, Gladstone, Roeland Park -> /, /about", "Customer project examples: railings, range hoods, wine shelving, stair railings -> /, /about", "Customer types: residential, commercial, industrial -> /, /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cm-fabricating' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='CWR Hawaii Inc has operated as a locally owned rigging specialist in Honolulu, Hawaii since 1976. The company serves the Hawaiian islands and the broader Pacific Rim from its Honolulu base.

The shop functions as a full-line rigging fabricator and service provider. It maintains the largest wire rope swage press in the state and produces custom wire rope, chain, synthetic, and high-performance slings with working loads up to 500,000 pounds. The company also operates an authorized repair station for brands such as Harrington Hoists, Ingersoll-Rand, JET, and Columbus-McKinnon, and offers wire rope pressure lubrication via Kirkpatrick systems. Rental inventory includes wireless load cells ranging from 2.5 to 55 tons, a 6.5-ton Bluetooth load cell, and a Straightpoint Colt tension meter.

CWR Hawaii supports marine, industrial, and material-handling customers across the Pacific. Its fabrication and repair services meet OSHA and ASME standards, and the company provides onsite consultation, certified product training, and same-day turnaround for many fabrication requests.

The company emphasizes its local presence, ISO 9001 certification, and the ability to deploy personnel and equipment to job sites the same day. Its differentiators include the state''s largest swage press, OEM-certified repair technicians, and a stock of rigging hardware that enables immediate shipment or fabrication.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom fabrication of wire rope, chain, synthetic, and high-performance slings", "Same-day fabrication service", "Wire rope swaging up to 500,000 lbs working load", "In-shop and onsite resin pour sockets for marine applications", "Proof load testing (static and dynamic) up to 25 tons for hoists", "Authorized repair of manual, electric, and pneumatic hoists and winches", "Wire rope pressure lubrication using Kirkpatrick systems", "Load cell rental (2.5 to 55 tons, wireless and Bluetooth)", "Pad eye tester rental", "Straightpoint Colt wire rope tension meter rental", "Onsite consultation and support", "Certified training for rigging products", "Proof testing up to 750,000 lbs"], "industries": ["Marine", "Industrial", "Material handling"], "materials": ["Wire rope", "Synthetic web", "Rope", "Chain", "High-performance slings", "Aluminum alloy castings", "Aerospace grade aluminium"], "equipment": ["Wire rope swage press (largest in Hawaii)", "Kirkpatrick Wire Rope Lubrication Systems", "Straightpoint Colt wire rope tension meter", "Bluetooth load cell (6.5 ton)", "Wireless load cells (2.5\u201355 tons)", "Pad eye tester"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day fabrication service available", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Largest wire rope swage press in Hawaii", "Authorized repair station for Harrington, Ingersoll-Rand, JET, Columbus-McKinnon", "Onsite resin pour sockets with Crosby Wirelock resin (ready in 60 minutes)", "Same-day fabrication service and onsite support"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1976 -> db", "Headquarters Honolulu, Hawaii -> db", "Locally owned -> homepage (/)", "ISO 9001 certified -> homepage (/) and db", "Largest wire rope swage press in Hawaii -> /services", "Fabricate slings up to 500,000 lbs working load -> /services", "Proof testing up to 750,000 lbs -> homepage (/) ", "Authorized repair station for Harrington, Ingersoll-Rand, JET, Columbus-McKinnon -> /services", "Hoist testing up to 25 tons -> /services", "Wire rope pressure lubrication with Kirkpatrick systems -> /services", "Load cell rentals 2.5-55 tons wireless, 6.5 ton Bluetooth -> /services", "Straightpoint Colt tension meter rental -> /services", "Pad eye tester rental -> /services", "Onsite resin pour sockets with Crosby Wirelock resin -> /services", "Same-day fabrication service -> /services", "Onsite consultation and support -> /services", "Certified training for products -> homepage (/) ", "Serves marine applications -> /services", "Meets OSHA and ASME standards -> /services", "Serves Pacific Rim -> homepage (/) ", "Materials: wire rope, synthetic web, rope, chain -> /services", "Aluminum alloy castings for Lug-All hoists -> db (capabilities)", "Aerospace grade aluminium for load cells -> /services"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cwr-hawaii-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Cable Associates was founded in 1989 in Archbald, Pennsylvania, as a U.S.-based cable manufacturer focused on quality, competitive pricing, customer service, and quick turnaround. The company began with a staff of under 10 and has grown to over 100 employees while maintaining its original core principles.

The company specializes in custom cable assemblies, including wire harnesses, fiber optic, copper, and RF cable assemblies, as well as contract manufacturing services. Its production capabilities encompass cutting, stripping, crimping, soldering, fiber polishing, epoxy dispensing, and comprehensive testing using equipment such as Schleuniger and Komax cut-and-strip machines, TE and Molex crimp presses, and Viavi optical test systems. All electrical assemblies undergo 100% continuity and signal integrity testing, while fiber optic and RF assemblies are tested to customer-specific requirements.

Cable Associates serves a diverse set of industries: military and aerospace (supplying defense contractors such as Leonardo DRS and Lockheed Martin), communications and telecom (supporting broadband expansion, FTTX, and data center upgrades), industrial, utilities (transmission and distribution networks), energy (wind, solar, electrical), medical (UL-rated assemblies), automotive (UL-rated harnesses), and agriculture (vehicle and machinery harnesses).

The company attributes its 35-plus-year customer retention to its unwavering commitment to U.S. manufacturing, quality certifications (AS9003, ITAR, UL, IPC standards), and rapid turnaround. It also holds an MMC Certification for hyperscale AI connectivity and is an authorized distributor for Microcare Sticklers fiber optic cleaning products.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9003','ITAR','UL Component - Processed Wire E514038','UL Processed Wire E514038','REACH','RoHS','IPC J-STD-001','IPC/WHMA-A-620','MMC Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assembly manufacturing", "Custom wire harness assembly", "Fiber optic cable assembly", "Copper cable assembly", "RF cable assembly", "Contract manufacturing", "Build-to-print manufacturing", "Cable cutting and stripping (Schleuniger, Komax)", "Crimping (TE, Molex, Positronic, Hirose, Amphenol)", "Soldering (JBC, Weller, Metcal)", "Solder pot operations", "Cable testing (Cirris, Fluke, Schleuniger)", "Fiber optic polishing (Domaille, SGI)", "Fiber optic epoxy dispensing (Nordson Performus III)", "Temperature controlled curing", "Optical testing (Viavi, Noyes, Opto-Test, EXFO, Rifocs)", "Fiber inspection (Viavi scopes, Daisy D-Scope MT)", "OTDR testing (Anritsu)", "Interferometry (Daisy, Norland, DORC)", "Clean-blast cleaning", "Labeling (Panduit, Brady, TE)", "First article inspection (AS9102B)", "BOM verification", "Drawing revision verification", "RoHS compliance verification"], "industries": ["Military / Aerospace", "Communications", "Telecom", "Industrial", "Utilities", "Energy", "Medical", "Automotive", "Agriculture"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Schleuniger Mercury 4 Laser Wire Strippers", "Schleuniger cut and strip machines", "Komax cut and strip machines", "TE, Molex, Positronic, Hirose, Amphenol crimp presses and tooling", "JBC, Weller, Metcal soldering stations", "Hexacon & AB Industrial solder pots", "Cirris & Fluke cable test systems", "Custom assembly and test fixtures", "Panduit, Brady, TE