UPDATE companies SET description='Chicago Plastic Systems is headquartered in Neenah, Wisconsin, with a second facility in Crystal Lake, Illinois. The company was founded in September 1995 by three businessmen—Dirk Howell, John Stewart, and Leif Heggem—who started in Howell’s garage producing CPVC fittings for the metal finishing industry. The business is veteran-owned.

The company specializes in industrial thermoplastic fabrication, offering plastic machining, plastic welding, custom fabrication of tanks, process skids, pipe systems, ductwork, enclosures, and corrosion-resistant ventilation equipment. Operations span 107,000 square feet across two locations, with a staff of approximately 50 employees. Fabricators are DVS certified or in certification, and the shop includes multiple CNC machines, a large CNC butt welder, and one of the largest brake presses dedicated to plastic bending.

Chicago Plastic Systems serves industries including metal finishing, water treatment, chemical processing, power generation, semiconductor, food, and pharmaceutical manufacturing. Customers range from OEMs needing custom thermoplastic components to plants requiring integrated installation and maintenance of fabricated systems.

The founders established the company on a philosophy of servant leadership, emphasizing dignity, honesty, and trust in relationships with customers, vendors, and employees. The firm highlights its commitment to DVS certification for all fabricators—a distinction it claims is unique in the U.S.—and a team-based culture built on employee referrals and long-tenured staff.', certifications=ARRAY['Veteran Owned Business']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic machining", "Plastic welding", "Custom plastic fabrication", "Industrial pipe fabrication", "Process skid fabrication", "Tank fabrication", "Plastic duct and fittings fabrication", "Corrosive ventilation systems", "Plastic enclosures and cabinets", "CNC machining", "CNC butt welding", "Plastic bending (brake press)", "Design assistance", "Material selection", "Installation and maintenance"], "industries": ["Metal finishing", "Water treatment", "Chemical processing", "Power generation", "Semiconductor", "Food processing", "Pharmaceutical"], "materials": ["PVC", "CPVC", "Polypropylene (Polypro)", "PVDF", "UHMW", "Delrin/Acetal", "Nylon", "PTFE (Teflon)", "PEEK", "Ultem", "Radel", "Polycarbonate", "PETG"], "equipment": ["CNC machines", "Large CNC butt welder", "Large brake press for plastic"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All fabricators DVS certified or in certification process", "107,000 sq ft facility with large brake press dedicated to plastic", "Veteran-owned business", "Engineers on staff for material selection and design assistance", "Founded on servant leadership philosophy"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Neenah, WI and Crystal Lake, IL -> /about-us", "Founded September 1995 by Dirk Howell, John Stewart, Leif Heggem -> /about-us", "Started in garage producing CPVC fittings -> /about-us", "Veteran-owned business -> / (home page) and db", "107,000 sq ft facility -> /about-us", "~50 employees -> db", "DVS certified fabricators -> /about-us", "CNC machines, large CNC butt