UPDATE companies SET description='Cirtronics Corporation, a contract manufacturer based in Milford, New Hampshire, was founded in 1979 by Gerardine Ferlins. Ferlins aimed to build a company that valued people as much as profits, extending that focus to customers, community, and suppliers. The company operates under an Employee Stock Ownership Plan (ESOP), making every employee a part-owner.

The company provides end-to-end manufacturing services for complex electromechanical systems, including engineering support, supply chain management, production, testing, logistics, and repair and refurbishment. Its capabilities span full system integration, complex sub-assemblies, and board-level assembly. Cirtronics emphasizes lean manufacturing practices, with green belts on staff, and uses an integrated IT platform to deliver real-time production information and work instructions.

Cirtronics serves the robotics, medical and life sciences, defense and security, and industrial markets. Its customer base includes Ava Robotics, Image Stream Medical, Doble Engineering, Heller Industries, Rapiscan Systems, and Belmont Medical Technologies. The company also operates as a repair depot and refurbishment center, housing spares and providing upgrades for deployed products.

Cirtronics differentiates itself through its employee-ownership culture, which it says aligns the interests of customers and staff, fostering better communication and dedicated teamwork. The company''s "Precision Engagement" approach tailors manufacturing programs to each client, and its quality management system monitors key processes with statistical process control. A focus on design for manufacturability and supplier qualification aims to reduce total cost of ownership.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','ITAR Registered','FDA Registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering support", "Supply chain management", "Production and assembly", "Testing and inspection", "Logistics and direct fulfillment", "Repair and refurbishment", "Transition to manufacturing (NPI)", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "System integration", "Sub-assembly build", "Board-level assembly", "Supplier qualification program", "Change management", "Training and mentoring (The Learning Center)", "Statistical process control (SPC)", "Quality management system (QMS)", "IT infrastructure integration"], "industries": ["Robotics", "Medical and Life Sciences", "Defense and Security", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee-owned ESOP structure aligning customer and employee interests", "Precision Engagement\u00ae tailored manufacturing programs", "Lean manufacturing with certified green belts on staff", "Integrated IT platform for real-time production data and work instructions", "Repair and refurbishment depot with spares housing and upgrade services"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1979 by Gerardine Ferlins -> /about-us", "Headquarters Milford, New Hampshire -> / (homepage) and /about-us", "Employee-owned ESOP -> /about-us and / (homepage)", "Certifications: ISO 9001, ISO 13485, ITAR Registered, FDA Registered -> /about-us and /quality", "Industries served: Robotics, Medical and Life Sciences, Defense and Security, Industrial -> / (homepage) and /about-us", "Capabilities: Engineering, Supply Chain, Production, Testing, Logistics, Repair and Refurbishment, Transition to Manufacturing, DFM -> / (homepage) and /about-us", "Customers: Ava Robotics, Image Stream Medical, Doble Engineering, Heller Industries, Rapiscan Systems, Belmont Medical Technologies -> / (homepage) and /about-us and /quality", "Lean manufacturing with green belts -> /quality", "Integrated IT platform for real-time information -> /quality", "Precision Engagement approach -> / (homepage)", "Repair depot and refurbishment center with spares housing -> / (homepage) description", "Quality management system with SPC -> /quality", "Training via The Learning Center -> /quality"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cirtronics-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Claremont Foods was founded in 2011 in Westminster, Colorado, as a family-owned food manufacturing company. The business was started by Alex (CEO), his wife Allison (Controller), and Alex’s two brothers, Adam (CFO) and Greg (Board Member). The family’s passion for healthy eating and commitment to quality and excellence shaped the company’s culture from the outset.

The company operates a 135,000-square-foot, state-of-the-art manufacturing facility where it provides a full suite of services: product innovation and development, materials sourcing, production and manufacturing, and product quality management. In-house capabilities include bench-top formulations, raw-material sourcing, costing analysis, line trials on existing equipment, packaging design, and access to external consultants. The team specializes in developing and producing energy bars, protein bars, and nutrition bars, using a transparent, volume-based tolling pricing model.

Claremont serves well-established brands in the food and natural-products industries that have national distribution. Its client base includes companies seeking new product development, cost reduction through re-formulation, packaging modifications, or process improvements, and quality enhancement of existing products. The company positions itself as an extension of the brand’s manufacturing division, handling supply-chain management so clients can focus on marketing and sales.

The founders emphasize mutual success, trust, and transparency as core differentiators. Because the family owners are directly involved in daily operations, clients interact with decision makers. The location adjacent to Boulder County—known as the heart of the natural-products industry—provides access to collective expertise, resources, and emerging innovations. A quality-assurance department staffed by SQF- and PCQI-certified professionals oversees every production shift.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF','PCQI']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product Innovation & Development", "Materials Sourcing", "Production & Manufacturing", "Product Quality Management", "In-house bench top formulations", "Raw materials sourcing", "Costing analysis", "Line trials on existing production equipment", "Packaging design", "Access to external consultants", "Cost reduction of existing products (re-formulations, packaging modifications, production process improvements)", "Quality improvement of existing products", "Development of new products"], "industries": ["Food manufacturing", "Natural products", "Energy bars", "Protein bars", "Nutrition bars"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned with direct access to decision makers", "135,000 sq ft state-of-the-art manufacturing facility", "Transparent volume-based tolling pricing model", "SQF and PCQI certified quality-assurance team", "Proximity to Boulder County natural-products ecosystem"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2011 -> db", "Family-owned -> /, /about", "Founders: Alex (CEO), Allison (Controller), Adam (CFO), Greg (Board Member) -> /about", "Headquarters: Westminster, Colorado -> db", "135,000 sq ft facility -> /services", "SQF certification -> db, /services", "PCQI certified professionals -> /services", "Services: product innovation, materials sourcing, production, quality management -> /services", "Specializes in energy bars, protein bars, nutrition bars -> /services", "Serves well-established brands with national distribution -> /about", "Business model: manufacturing division, transparent volume-based tolling -> /about, /services", "Located adjacent to Boulder County natural products hub -> /about", "Mutual success, trust, transparency as differentiators -> /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='claremont-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Classic Packaging Company operates from Pfafftown, North Carolina, where it has been family-owned and operated since its founding in 1991. The company began as a flexible packaging provider focused on delivering high-quality plastic packaging solutions to retailers, food processors, and distributors nationwide.

The company specializes in flexographic printing, laminating, coating, slitting, pouching, and bag making, supported by pre-press services and in-house lab testing. Its production floor runs 10-color PCMC flexographic presses with AVT 100% inspection, solventless single-component laminators from Nordmechanica and Comexi, and servo-driven pouch lines equipped with leak testers on every station. Additional capabilities include the Hudson-Sharp EZ-Stand system for pre-gusseted stand-up pouches and the INNO-LOK pre-zippered fastener application.

Classic Packaging serves retailers, food processors, and packaging distributors across the United States. Its food-grade, FDA-approved packaging is used for frozen foods, snacks, sweets, pet foods, frozen poultry, baking mixes, frozen vegetables, frozen seafood, and coffee.

The company states its mission is to create business relationships where all participants prosper, emphasizing honesty, integrity, a safe workplace, and environmental stewardship. It differentiates itself through continuous technological investment, rigorous quality control during lamination and printing, and proprietary equipment configurations that enable faster filling speeds and reduced waste.', certifications=ARRAY['FDA approved (food-grade)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Flexographic printing (10-color PCMC)", "Laminating (solventless, single-component)", "Coating (heat seal, cold seal, barrier, varnish)", "Slitting (cantilevered, duplex slitter rewinders, folding, perforating, Inno-lok zipper installation)", "Pouching (three-side seal, stand-up pouches with/without zippers, tear notches, hang holes)", "Bag making (printed, laminated, wicketed, flat, zipper, hook, gusseted, grommeted, random/registered inline printing, hot melt, resealable tape, punches, perforations)", "Pre-press services", "Lab testing", "INNO-LOK application", "EZ-Stand application"], "industries": ["Retailers", "Food processors", "Packaging distributors"], "materials": ["Plastic films", "Food-grade materials", "Barrier films", "Non-barrier films", "Printed roll stock"], "equipment": ["Hudson-Sharp EZ-Stand machine", "Hudson-Sharp INNO-LOK machine", "Nordmechanica laminators", "Comexi laminators", "10-color PCMC flexographic printing presses", "AVT 100% inspection system", "X-rite color matching software", "Servo-driven pouch equipment with leak testers", "Cantilevered slitting process with duplex slitter rewinders"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["FDA-approved food-grade packaging", "Hudson-Sharp EZ-Stand for pre-gusseted stand-up pouches", "Hudson-Sharp INNO-LOK pre-zippered fastener application", "10-color PCMC flexographic printing with AVT 100% inspection", "Solventless single-component lamination using Nordmechanica and Comexi laminators"], "facts_used": ["Family-owned since 1991 -> /", "Headquarters in Pfafftown, North Carolina -> db", "Founded in 1991 -> db", "FDA approved certification -> db", "Flexographic printing, laminating, coating, slitting, pouching, bag making, lab testing, pre-press -> /", "10-color PCMC flexographic presses with AVT 100% inspection -> /", "Solventless single-component lamination with Nordmechanica and Comexi laminators -> /", "Hudson-Sharp EZ-Stand for stand-up pouches -> /", "Hudson-Sharp INNO-LOK pre-zippered fastener -> /", "Servo-driven pouch equipment with leak testers -> /", "Cantilevered slitting with duplex slitter rewinders -> /", "Coating options: heat seal, cold seal, barrier, varnish -> /", "Bag making variations: printed, laminated, wicketed, flat, zipper, hook, gusseted, grommeted, inline printing, hot melt, resealable tape, punches, perforations -> /", "Pouch types: three-side seal, stand-up with/without zippers, tear notches, hang holes -> /", "Industries served: retailers, food processors, packaging distributors -> /", "Applications: frozen foods, snacks, sweets, pet foods, frozen poultry, baking mixes, frozen vegetables, frozen seafood, coffee -> /", "Mission: create relationships where all participants prosper, honesty, integrity, safe workplace, environmental stewardship -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='classic-packaging-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Classic Sheet Metal was founded in March 1962 in a 7,500-square-foot facility in Chicago, Illinois. The company relocated to Schiller Park in the late 1960s, then to a 30,000-square-foot plant where it operated for three decades before moving to its current headquarters in Addison, Illinois, in 2000.

The company provides turnkey sheet metal fabrication including CNC punching, laser cutting, stamping, forming, welding, and contract assembly. It runs both short-run (custom or urgent turnaround) and long-run production, with stated capacity ranging from prototype quantities to several million pieces annually. The facility operates under an ISO 9001:2015 quality management system and employs statistical process control (SPC) with decades of accumulated process data.

Classic Sheet Metal serves as a supply-chain partner for several well-known global companies across a broad geographic footprint that includes the Midwest, South, and Mountain West regions.

The firm was established on the premise that quality and customer service are the cornerstones of excellence. It differentiates itself through early adoption of SPC, a Virtek Laser QC automated inspection system capable of ±0.05 mm accuracy, and a suite of quality tools including PPAP, FMEA, Six Sigma, and just-in-time delivery programs.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC Punching", "CNC Laser Cutting", "Metal Stamping", "Metal Forming", "Welding Services", "Contract Assembly", "Hardware Installation", "Design & Engineering Consulting", "First Article Inspection (Virtek Laser QC)", "Statistical Process Control (SPC)", "PPAP", "FMEA", "RoHS Compliance", "Kanban/LEAN", "Just-in-Time Delivery", "Six Sigma", "Certificate of Compliance", "Electronic Data Interchange (EDI)"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Virtek Laser QC automated inspection system"], "volume": "Prototype runs to several million pieces annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "\u00b10.05 mm (0.002 in) inspection accuracy (Virtek Laser QC)", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 registered quality management system", "Pioneers in statistical process control (SPC) with decades of process data", "Virtek Laser QC automated inspection with \u00b10.05 mm accuracy", "Turnkey fabrication from punching and laser cutting through welding and assembly", "Short-run and long-run production with just-in-time delivery capability"], "facts_used": ["Founded March 1962 in 7,500 sq ft Chicago facility -> /about", "Relocated to Schiller Park (12,000 sq ft) late 1960s -> /about", "Operated 30,000 sq ft facility for 30 years -> /about", "Moved to current Addison, IL location in 2000 -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 registered quality management system -> /quality", "Turnkey capabilities: punching, laser cutting, stamping, forming, welding, assembly -> /, /quality", "Short-run and long-run production -> /, /about", "Capacity: prototype to several million pieces annually -> produ