UPDATE companies SET description='Cork Medical was founded in 2007 in Indianapolis, Indiana, by a team of founders who set out to improve lives through innovative wound care solutions. The company began as a distributor of negative pressure wound therapy (NPWT) devices and specialty mattresses before evolving into a manufacturer with its own clinical and engineering teams.

Today, Cork Medical designs and manufactures the Nisus NPWT System, specialty mattresses, overlays, and wheelchair cushions. The company’s product development is driven by clinician input, resulting in what it describes as one of the industry’s most reliable and powerful NPWT platforms. Its products are sold worldwide.

The company serves healthcare institutions including hospitals, nursing homes, long-term care facilities, and homecare agencies, as well as distributors seeking cost-effective NPWT solutions. Cork Medical identifies as a medical device and support surface manufacturer.

Cork Medical’s stated mission is to improve lives through innovative wound care products, with a vision to become a global manufacturer in the field. The company cites its ISO 13485:2016 certification and clinician-driven product development as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Negative Pressure Wound Therapy (NPWT) system design and manufacturing", "Specialty mattress and support surface manufacturing", "Wheelchair cushion manufacturing", "Clinical and engineering product development", "Global distribution and sales"], "industries": ["Medical Device Manufacturing", "Support Surface Manufacturing", "Healthcare", "Long-term Care", "Home Healthcare"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Nisus NPWT System: powerful, cost-effective negative pressure wound therapy", "Products developed by clinicians for clinicians", "ISO 13485:2016 certified quality management", "Global distribution network", "In-house clinical and engineering teams"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2007 -> /about", "Headquartered in Indianapolis, Indiana -> db", "ISO 13485:2016 certified -> /", "Manufactures NPWT systems, specialty mattresses, overlays, and cushions -> /", "Started as distributor of NPWT and specialty mattresses -> /about", "Developed Nisus NPWT System -> /about", "Serves hospitals, nursing homes, long-term care, homecare facilities -> /about", "Mission: improve lives through innovative wound care products -> /about", "Vision: leading global manufacturer of wound care products -> /about", "Core values: Energetic to Achieve, Hard work with balance, Compassionate -> /about"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='cork-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='County Auto Salvage LLC was founded in 2020 in Claymont, Delaware. The company operates as a nationwide distributor of used OEM automotive parts, sourcing from a network of over 200 Automotive Recyclers Association (ARA) certified salvage yards across the United States and Canada.

The company supplies complete engines, transmissions, transfer cases, body panels, lighting, suspension components, electronic modules, and other recycled OEM parts. Each part undergoes multi-point inspection, compression testing, and VIN-matched fitment verification before being shipped via LTL and freight with tracking. The business employs 11 to 50 people and manages an e-commerce platform for direct distribution.

County Auto Salvage emphasizes transparency by including all shipping costs in listed prices, offers a 30-day return policy, provides round-the-clock customer support, and maintains an extensive inventory spanning numerous makes and models.', certifications=ARRAY['ARA (Automotive Recyclers Association) Certified Supplier Network','OEM Quality Replacement Standards','Pre-Inspection & Verification Protocols']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Nationwide OEM Recycled Auto Parts Sourcing", "Direct VIN Matching & Fitment Verification", "Rigorous Multi-Point Part Inspection & Compression Testing", "Nationwide LTL & Freight Shipping with Tracking", "30-Day Limited Parts Replacement Warranty", "Dedicated Automotive Parts Specialist Customer Support", "E-Commerce Salvage Parts Distribution"], "industries": ["Automotive Repair & Service Shops", "Collision & Auto Body Centers", "Fleet Maintenance & Commercial Vehicles", "Automotive Enthusiasts & DIY Restorers", "Insurance Claim Replacement"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Included shipping costs in product prices with no hidden fees", "30-day return policy on all parts", "VIN-matched fitment verification for accurate part selection", "Network of 200+ ARA-certified salvage yards across U.S. and Canada"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2020 -> db", "Headquartered in Claymont, Delaware -> db", "Employee count 11-50 -> db", "Partners with over 200 ARA-certified salvage yards -> db", "Supplies used OEM parts including engines, transmissions, body panels, etc. -> db", "Multi-point inspection, VIN matching, compression testing -> db", "Nationwide LTL and freight shipping with tracking -> db", "30-day limited parts replacement warranty -> db", "Industries served: automotive repair shops, collision centers, fleet maintenance, enthusiasts, insurance claims -> db", "Included shipping costs in product prices -> /", "30-day return policy -> /", "24/7 customer support -> /", 