UPDATE companies SET description='Craftech Plastics was founded in 1979 in Anaheim, California, as a mold-making shop. The US-owned company operates a twin-plant model with facilities in Anaheim and Tijuana, Mexico, providing design optimization, engineering, tooling, and injection molding services under one management structure.

Today the company runs 45-plus injection molding machines ranging from 38 to 750 tons across 110,000 square feet of production space. Its capabilities span consultative engineering, mold flow analysis, in-house toolroom construction (including multi-action and hot-runner molds), and specialized molding such as elastomeric overmolding, insert molding, multi-component molding, and high-temperature molding. Both plants feature ISO Class 8 and Class 7 cleanrooms for medical-grade production, complemented by value-added operations including cleanroom assembly, ultrasonic welding, laser degating, decoration, and packaging.

Craftech serves medical device, consumer product, high-technology, and industrial markets. Its customer base includes a Global 1000 medical diagnostics OEM, a solar energy manufacturer, ophthalmology specialist CZM, and a major industrial technology OEM that has partnered with Craftech for over 20 years. The company supports programs from early design-for-manufacturability reviews through IQ/OQ/PQ validation for regulated medical components, as well as medium-volume runs for handheld electronics and consumer appliances.

The firm emphasizes a relationship-driven approach built on four core values—passion, integrity, accountability, and continuous improvement. Its structured ''Craftech Process'' moves projects through Discover, Engage, and Fulfill phases with cross-functional kickoff meetings, risk scoring, and ongoing program management. Leadership cites the twin-plant footprint, combined 250-plus years of mold-making expertise, and single-source responsibility from design to validated production as key differentiators that have retained clients for decades.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','UL Registered (Yellow Card)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Consultative engineering services", "Cross-functional design reviews", "Part design refinement", "Mold flow analysis (CAE)", "Mold design", "Mold construction", "In-house toolroom", "Domestic mold making", "Offshore mold making", "Multi-action molds", "Hot runner molds", "Custom injection molding", "Elastomeric overmolding", "Insert molding", "Multi-component molding", "High temperature molding", "Scientific molding", "Process capability studies", "Metrology", "Cleanroom molding (ISO Class 8/7)", "Cleanroom assembly (whiteroom)", "Ultrasonic welding", "Laser degating", "Decoration and screen printing"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Consumer Products", "High-Technology", "Industrial", "Diagnostics", "Biopharmaceuticals", "Ophthalmology", "Solar Energy", "Electronics"], "materials": ["Thermoplastic polymers (wide range)"], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines (38\u2013750 ton range, 45+ units)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Twin-plant operations in Anaheim, CA and Tijuana, Mexico", "ISO Class 8 and 7 cleanrooms at both facilities", "In-house toolroom with domestic and offshore mold-making options", "Scientific molding with process capability studies and metrology", "Lean manufacturing and continuous improvement culture"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1979 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Anaheim, California -> /about-us", "Twin-plant facilities in Anaheim and Tijuana, Mexico -> /about-us", "Total 110,000 sq ft production space -> /about-us", "45+ injection molding machines, 38-750 tons -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 13485:2016 certifications across both facilities -> /about-us", "UL registered -> /about-us", "Cleanroom Class 8 and 7 capabilities -> / and /about-us", "In-house toolroom with domestic/offshore options -> /capabilities", "250+ years combined mold-making experience -> /capabilities", "Consultative engineering, cross-functional design reviews, mold flow analysis -> / and /capabilities", "Specialized molding: elastomeric overmolding, insert molding, multi-component, high-temp -> /", "Value-added: cleanroom assembly, ultrasonic welding, laser degating, decoration -> /", "Industries served: Medical Devices, Consumer Products, High-Technology, Industrial -> /", "Customer examples: Global 1000 medical diagnostics OEM, solar energy leader, CZM ophthalmology, industrial technology OEM -> /", "Medium-volume production runs for handheld electronics -> /", "IQ/OQ/PQ validation support for medical -> /", "Core values: passion, integrity, accountability, continuous improvement -> /about-us", "Craftech Process: Discover, Engage, Fulfill phases -> /about-us", "Lean manufacturing, APQP, Six Sigma -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='craftech-plastic-injection-molding-mold-making-tooling-and-engineering-for-medical-and-hi-technology-in-usa-mexico' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Curtis Industries, based in Milwaukee, Wisconsin, traces its roots to 1933 when it began as a manufacturer of electrical components.

The company produces a broad line of standard and custom electrical components, including barrier and PCB terminal blocks, EMI/RFI power line filters, TRI-MAG power supplies, and custom molded assemblies. Manufacturing is performed in-house across multiple sites in Wisconsin, Arizona, Mexico, and China, encompassing plastic injection molding, transfer molding, fabrication, and rigorous testing using equipment such as an Agilent E7402A emissions analyzer.

Curtis serves OEMs and distributors in industrial instrumentation, power supply, telecommunications, medical, commercial appliance, machinery, aerospace, military, and networking sectors. Its customer base includes global 1000 organizations that rely on the firm for new product introduction support, PCB assembly, cable assemblies, system integration, and supply chain logistics.

Quality is described as the founding principle of the business. Curtis holds ISO 9001:2015 certification, ITAR registration, and UL, CSA, and TUV safety approvals. The company emphasizes an first-pass yield on new designs, achieved through optimized engineering methodology and process control, and offers engineering design-in and material outsourcing to help clients reduce cost of goods sold.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR','UL','CSA','TUV']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom electrical component design", "Barrier terminal block manufacturing", "PCB terminal block manufacturing", "Euro-style barrier strip manufacturing", "High-voltage/high-current terminal block manufacturing", "EMI/RFI power line filter manufacturing (single-phase, three-phase, DC, medical)", "Power entry module manufacturing", "TRI-MAG power supply manufacturing", "Custom plastic injection molding", "Transfer molding", "Fabrication and assembly", "Emissions testing (Agilent E7402A)", "Pre-compliance testing", "PCB assembly", "Cable assembly", "System integration", "Supply chain logistics and order fulfillment", "Engineering design-in services", "Material outsourcing"], "industries": ["Industrial Instrumentation", "Power Supplies", "Telecommunications", "Medical", "Commercial", "Appliance", "Machinery", "Aerospace", "Military", "Networking", "Communications", "Industrial Controls"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Agilent E7402A emissions test system", "Isolated test environment", "Plastic injection molding machines", "Transfer molding equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Industry-leading first-pass yield on new designs", "Global manufacturing and inventory footprint in Wisconsin, Arizona, Mexico, and China", "Full in-house production from plastic injection molding through final test", "Engineering design-in and material outsourcing to lower COGS", "ISO 9001:2015, ITAR, UL, CSA, and TUV certifications"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1933 -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Milwaukee, Wisconsin -> db", "Division of Powers Holdings, Inc. -> /about-us", "Manufactures terminal blocks, EMI/RFI filters, power supplies, custom molded components -> /", "In-house manufacturing: plastic injection molding, transfer molding, fabrication, testing -> /", "Global facilities in Wisconsin, Arizona, Mexico, China -> /about-us", "Serves industrial instrumentation, power supplies, telecom, medical, commercial, appliance, machinery, aerospace, military, networking -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /about-us", "ITAR registered -> /about-us", "UL, CSA, TUV safety approvals -> /", "Industry-leading first-pass yield on new designs -> /", "Engineering design-in and material outsourcing -> /about-us", "Agilent E7402A emissions test equipment -> /", "Pre-compliance testing services -> /", "PCB assembly, cable assemblies, system integration, supply chain logistics -> /about-us"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='curtis-industries' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Fashion Atlas Group began in Kyiv, Ukraine in 2010 as a venture among four friends, including Kyrylo Kostiuchenko, who remains the owner. By 2014 the company expanded internationally, opening a U.S. office and warehouse in Bayonne, New Jersey in 2015. The business is privately owned and founder-led.

The company provides end-to-end apparel services: custom manufacturing, wholesale sourcing, private label production, product development, sampling, fabric sourcing, quality control, packaging, and logistics. It manages production across facilities in China, Turkey, and Ukraine, with warehouses in the U.S., England, Poland, Turkey, and Ukraine. The company reports 450+ partners worldwide, 350+ active suppliers, over 40 private label brands, and around 100,000 SKUs in stock. It handles orders from as low as 5 pieces for wholesale to 2,000+ pieces in two weeks for custom runs.

Fashion Atlas serves fashion brands, boutiques, online retailers, startups, and corporate clients needing uniforms or merchandise. Named clients include Shopakira, Altar’d State, Nordstrom, and Ruelala. Industries span sportswear, restaurant uniforms, protective clothing, military uniforms, corporate apparel, and general fashion.

The company emphasizes a managed workflow that connects sourcing, development, production, inspection, and delivery under one U.S.-based partner, offering safe payments, pre-shipment inspections, and flexible MOQs. It highlights global production control, ethical certifications (ISO 9001, Higg Index, BCI, GRS, SMETA), and a focus on reducing risk for brands entering apparel manufacturing.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','Higg Index','BCI','GRS','SMETA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom clothing manufacturing", "Wholesale apparel sourcing", "Private label production", "Product development and sampling", "Fabric and supplier sourcing", "Quality control and pre-shipment inspection", "Packaging and logistics", "Corporate apparel and merchandise", "Low MOQ manufacturing", "Product sourcing", "Supplier management", "Sampling and production management", "Branding and packaging customization", "Drop-ship and flash-sales fulfillment", "Bulk and off-price order options"], "industries": ["Fashion brands", "Boutiques", "Online retailers", "Startups", "Corporate clients", "Sportswear", "Restaurant uniforms", "Protective clothing", "Military uniforms", "Corporate apparel", "Medical clothing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Wholesale from 5 pieces per style; custom manufacturing from 50 pieces per style; production capacity of 2,000+ pieces within two weeks; 250M+ units manufactured historically", "lead_time": "In-stock items: 5 days delivery (or 48 hours for some); custom manufacturing: approximately 2 weeks for 2,000+ pieces", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["U.S.-based payments and legal protection", "Pre-shipment quality inspections by third parties", "Production scaling from low MOQs to large volumes", "Door-to-door global delivery from warehouses on three continents", "Flexible MOQs: 5 pieces for wholesale, 50 pieces for custom development"], "facts_used": ["Founded in Kyiv in 2010 by four friends including Kyrylo Kostiuchenko -> /about-us", "U.S. 