UPDATE companies SET description='Custom Coils operates from Alcester, South Dakota, where it was founded in 1967. The company manufactures custom transformers, inductors, and specialty magnetic components for a global customer base.

The 17,000-square-foot facility employs over 100 people and serves more than 140 active accounts, with no single account exceeding 16 percent of sales. Primary winding capabilities include complex hand winding, high-voltage layer winding, multi-spindle high-speed bobbin winding, and heavy-wire winding; the secondary area adds universal (pi) winding and toroid winding. Production test equipment comprises inductance analyzers, hipot testers, automated testers, and micro-ohm meters. The product range spans high-voltage, switchmode, flyback, trigger pulse, step-up/down, power, toroidal, and surface-mount transformers, as well as air-core, ferrite, and power inductors, antennas, air coils, DC igniters, and hydrogen coils.

Customers come from agriculture technology, heavy industrial, bio-medical devices, oil exploration and downhole, plasma generation, communications, aerospace and military, seismic exploration, high-tech mining, power distribution, semiconductor and electronics manufacturing, renewable energy and power generation, robotics and industrial automation, and automotive and electric vehicles.

The company emphasizes personalized service: engineers build their own samples, a key manager handles customer service, and top management visits every client. Custom Coils also offers reverse engineering to replace end-of-life components, custom prototyping, assisted design, and through-hole PCB assembly for up to 15 components. All products are manufactured in the United States.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Complex hand winding", "High-voltage layer winding", "Multi-spindle high-speed bobbin winding", "Heavy wire winding", "Universal (pi) winding", "Toroid winding", "Custom prototyping", "Assisted design services", "Custom test suite creation (Voltech AT3600)", "Through-hole PCB assembly (typically <15 components)", "Reverse engineering", "Custom winding (round magnet wire 10 GA to 44 GA)", "Component assembly for magnetic components", "Molding and encapsulation for magnetic components", "Transformer lamination", "Lead attachment for all coils", "Inductance analysis", "Hipot testing", "Automated testing", "Micro ohm measurement"], "industries": ["Agriculture Technology", "Heavy Industrial Applications", "Bio-Medical Devices", "Oil Exploration & Downhole Applications", "Plasma Generation", "Communication", "Aerospace and Military", "Seismic Exploration", "High Tech Mining", "Power Distribution", "Semiconductor & Electronics Manufacturing", "Renewable Energy & Power Generation", "Robotics & Industrial Automation", "Automotive & Electric Vehicles (EVs)"], "materials": ["Magnet wire (10-44 AWG)"], "equipment": ["High RPM multi-spindle winder", "Voltech AT3600 test system", "Inductance analyzers", "Hipot testers", "Automated testers", "Micro ohm meters"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Engineers build their own samples", "Dedicated key manager for customer service", "Top management visits all customers", "Reverse engineering for end-of-life components", "All products manufactured in the USA"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1967 -> db", "Headquarters Alcester, South Dakota -> db", "ISO 9001 certified -> db, /", "Facility size 17,000 sq ft -> /about-us", "Over 100 employees -> /about-us", "140+ active accounts, no account >16% sales -> /about-us", "Primary winding capabilities (hand wind, HV layer, multi-spindle bobbin, heavy wire) -> /about-us", "Secondary winding capabilities (universal pi, toroid) -> /about-us", "Production test equipment (inductance analyzers, hipot testers, automated testers, micro ohm meters) -> /about-us", "Product list (transformers, inductors, coils, antennas, DC igniters, hydrogen coils) -> /", "Industries served list -> /, /about-us", "Personalized service (engineers build samples, key manager, top management visits) -> /about-us", "Reverse engineering for end-of-life components -> /services", "Custom prototyping, assisted design, through-hole PCB assembly (<15 components) -> /services", "Custom winding range 10 GA to 44 GA -> /services", "Molding and encapsulation, transformer lamination, lead attachment -> /services", "High RPM multi-spindle winder added -> /", "Voltech AT3600 used for test suite -> /services", "Manufactured in USA -> /"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='custom-coils' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Custom Service Plastics, LLC (CSP) has operated from Lake Geneva, Wisconsin since 2000. The company occupies facilities totaling more than 200,000 square feet and is certified as a Woman Business Enterprise (WBE), a Minority Business Enterprise (MBE), and an SBA-designated Small Disadvantaged Business operating under the IATF 16949 quality management system.

The operation emphasizes cost efficiency and on-time delivery across its production floor, offering low-cost engineering support for diverse client needs.

Founded on a commitment to be a leader in custom molding partnerships, CSP focuses on timely, cost-effective solutions that add value within the customer-supplier relationship. The company states its reputation speaks for itself, built on capturing the minute details of each customer''s requirements.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic molding", "Engineering design support", "Quality management (IATF 16949)", "Manufacturing operations"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 200,000 sq ft of manufacturing space", "Woman-owned (WBE), minority-owned (MBE), SBA small disadvantaged business", "IATF 16949 quality management system", "Complete engineering solutions at low cost"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2000 -> db", "Headquarters in Lake Geneva, Wisconsin -> db", "Facilities over 200,000 sq ft -> page:/", "Woman Business Enterprise (WBE) certification -> page:/", "Minority Business Enterprise (MBE) certification -> page:/", "SBA Small Disadvantaged Business designation -> page:/", "IATF 16949 quality management system -> db, page:/", "Custom plastic molding services -> page:/", "Engineering solutions offered -> page:/", "Team includes engineering, quality, manufacturing associates -> page:/", "Serves Fortune 500 companies worldwide -> page:/", "Commitment to custom molding partnerships -> page:/", "Focus on timely, cost-effective solutions -> page:/", "Emphasis on capturing minute details of customer requirements -> page:/"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='custom-service-plastics-inc-corporate-headquarters' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='DCA Manufacturing, headquartered in Troy, Michigan, was founded in 1981 under the name Debron Industrial Electronics. The company maintains multi-site operations across Michigan and Wisconsin, anchoring its presence in the Midwest''s manufacturing corridor.

The company provides end-to-end electronics manufacturing services, including printed circuit board assembly (PCBA), system design and engineering, smart supply chain management, system integration and box build, inspection and testing, and turnkey solutions. With over four decades of experience and a team accumulating 290 years of cumulative technical expertise, DCA operates multiple manufacturing locations in the Midwest, though specific facility sizes and headcount are not disclosed.

DCA serves customers in defense and aerospace, industrial, medical and healthcare, automotive, power and energy, and emerging technology sectors. The company references serving marquee customers across these industries, though specific client names are not disclosed.

DCA emphasizes its financial stability, with over four decades of consistent profitability enabling reinvestment in technology and talent. Its customer-centric culture assigns dedicated program managers to each project, while its integrated manufacturing model eliminates multiple vendors and accelerates time-to-market. The company also highlights its global supply chain network with real-time analytics, customized on-shoring solutions for U.S.-based production, and a geographic advantage in the Midwest''s manufacturing corridor.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','IATF 16949','RoHS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed Circuit Board Assembly (PCBA)", "System Design & Engineering", "Smart Supply Chain Management", "System Integration & Box Build", "Inspection & Testing", "Turn-Key Solutions", "Component-Level Repairs", "Firmware and Hardware Upgrades", "Proactive Component Monitoring", "Alternative Component Sourcing", "End-of-Life (EOL) Component Sourcing", "Design Validation and Engineering Support", "Component Procurement", "Final Assembly and Testing"], "industries": ["Defense & Aerospace", "Industrial", "Medical & Healthcare", "Automotive", "Power & Energy", "Emerging Technologies"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Limited prototypes to expansive production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Four decades of consistent profitability funding technology reinvestment", "Dedicated program managers for each customer project", "Full product life-cycle management under one integrated workflow", "Global supply chain network with real-time data analytics", "U.S.-based on-shoring solutions reducing lead times and geopolitical risk"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1981 as Debron Industrial Electronics -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Troy, Michigan -> db", "Multi-site operations in Michigan and Wisconsin -> /about-us", "Certifications: ISO 9001, ISO 13485, IATF 16949, RoHS -> db", "Services: PCBA, system design & engineerin