UPDATE companies SET description='Decotex, Inc. is a privately owned U.S. company headquartered in Maple Grove, Minnesota, with a second office in Patterson, New York. Founded in 1985 as a distributor of nylon screen fabrics, the business has since expanded its product range to include filtration, belting, and industrial fabrics. It operates from two locations in Minnesota and New York, with sales representatives across North America, and conducts business worldwide.

The company develops woven fabric solutions for filtration and industrial applications. Decotex maintains multiple production facilities across North America, Europe, India, China, and Japan, all ISO 9001:2015 certified. Most screen and filter fabrics are stocked for immediate shipment, while belting items are made to order due to variable widths and lengths.

Decotex serves a broad range of industries, including water purification, wastewater treatment, mining and minerals, food and beverage, chemical and industrial processing, electrical appliance, and automotive filtration.

Decotex emphasizes product and technical knowledge, a low-overhead structure for competitive pricing, a large inventory of key fabrics enabling fast and same-day delivery, and the development of new fabrics to meet evolving customer needs. Its stated mission is to be a supplier of filtration and industrial woven and non-woven media while providing a high level of service and technical support.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Woven synthetic screen fabrics (monofilament, multifilament, knit)", "Filter fabrics (plain, Oxford, twill, basket, sateen, satin weaves)", "Woven and spiral belting (plain, spiral, twill, dual layer, satin weaves)", "Tubular woven fabrics (plain, twill, satin weaves)", "Coating and laminating substrate", "Custom fabric development", "Fabrication to size with closures"], "industries": ["Water purification", "Wastewater treatment", "Mining and minerals", "Food and beverage", "Chemical and industrial processing", "Electrical appliance", "Automotive filtration"], "materials": ["Nylon (PA)", "Polyester (PET)", "Polypropylene (PP)", "ETFE", "PVDF", "Acrylic", "Kevlar (aramid)", "Cotton", "Polyethylene", "PPS", "PTFE", "Stainless steel", "PEEK", "Carbon", "Copper", "Glass"], "equipment": ["Shuttle looms", "Needle looms"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping on stocked screen and filter fabrics; made-to-order belting per customer requirements", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Large inventory of key fabrics for immediate delivery", "Same-day shipment on stocked items", "Multiple production facilities across North America, Europe, and Asia", "ISO 9001:2015 certified plants", "Product and technical knowledge with custom fabric development"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1985 as distributor of nylon screen fabrics -> db", "Headquarters Maple Grove, Minnesota -> db", "Privately owned US based company -> /about-us", "Operates from two locations Minnesota and New York with sales reps across North America -> /a