UPDATE companies SET description='Delaware Manufacturing Extension Partnership (DEMEP) operates from Newark, Delaware, where it was established in 1994 as a federally and state funded non-profit organization. It serves as the official representative of the MEP National Network in Delaware, operating through Delaware Technical Community College in partnership with the U.S. Department of Commerce''s National Institute of Standards and Technology, the Delaware Division of Small Business, and state and local chambers of commerce.

Its core offerings include Lean Enterprise deployment, Quality Management Systems implementation, Statistical Approach and Six Sigma methodologies, Design of Experiments, Top Line Growth strategy, and Energy Savings Analysis and Audit.

The partnership serves Delaware''s manufacturing base across multiple sectors, along with financial institutions and health care and service providers. Its client engagements span automotive suppliers requiring ISO/TS 16949 compliance, medical device manufacturers needing ISO 13485 systems, and general manufacturers seeking lean transformation, quality certification, energy reduction, or market growth strategies.

