UPDATE companies SET description='Design Plastics Inc was founded in 1972 in Omaha, Nebraska, as a custom thermoforming business leveraging in-house tooling expertise. The company is now part of Coda Resources LTD.

The company provides custom injection molding, vacuum forming, and rotary thermoforming, supported by engineering and tooling services. Its injection molding presses range from 55 to 730 tons, and its thermoforming equipment handles sheets up to 5 feet by 9 feet and thicknesses from 0.080 to 0.50 inches. After forming, 3-axis and 6-axis CNC machines perform trimming. Operations run from two Nebraska facilities in Omaha and Blair, serving prototype through high-volume production.

Design Plastics serves OEMs in aerospace, automotive, agricultural, governmental, medical, retail, and industrial manufacturing sectors across the United States and international markets.

The company emphasizes its dual-process capability—injection molding and vacuum forming under one roof—allowing engineers to guide customers to the optimal process and remain involved through production. It highlights U.S.-based manufacturing, an ISO 9001-certified quality system, and sustainability initiatives including wind turbines and recycling.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Injection Molding", "Vacuum Forming", "Rotary Thermoforming (Multi-Station)", "Engineering & Design Support", "Tooling Design & Fabrication", "DFM Review", "Mold-Flow Analysis Coordination", "3-Axis CNC Trimming", "6-Axis CNC Trimming", "Prototyping", "Low-Volume Production", "High-Volume Production", "Single-Sheet Forming", "Material Selection Assistance", "3D Modeling"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Automotive", "Agricultural", "Governmental", "Medical", "Retail", "Industrial Manufacturing"], "materials": ["Thermoplastics"], "equipment": ["Injection Molding Presses (55-730 ton)", "Multi-Station Rotary Thermoforming Machine", "3-Axis CNC Machines", "6-Axis CNC Machines"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Combined injection molding and vacuum forming capabilities under one roof", "Engineers integrated into manufacturing operations for continuous design-to-production involvement", "ISO 9001 certified quality management system", "U.S.-based manufacturing with two Nebraska plants since 1972", "Sustainability initiatives including wind turbines and recycling"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1972 in Omaha, Nebraska -> /about-us", "Part of Coda Resources LTD -> /about-us", "Injection molding presses 55-730 tons -> /", "Thermoforming sheet size up to 5x9 ft, thickness .080-.50 in -> /", "3-axis and 6-axis CNC trimming -> /", "Two plants: Omaha and Blair, Nebraska -> /", "Industries served: aerospace, automotive, agricultural, governmental, medical, retail, industrial manufacturing -> db", "IS