UPDATE companies SET description='Direct Components Inc. operates from a 10,700-square-foot facility in Tampa, Florida, where it has been based since relocating in 2020. The company was founded on July 6, 1998, and has been under the sole ownership of Aaron Nursey since 2014.

The firm functions as an independent distributor of electronic components, focusing on hard-to-find, end-of-life, and obsolete parts for OEMs, contract manufacturers, and EMS providers. Its capabilities span semiconductor sourcing, excess inventory recovery through direct purchase, consignment, or brokered models, and a full in-house quality lab. The 2,000-square-foot climate-controlled lab and warehouse maintains ANSI/ESD S20.20 compliance and houses equipment including a Keyence VHX digital microscope, Creative Electron Truview Prime X-ray system, Hitachi XMET 8000, Mantis Elite microscope, and Tektronix 576 curve tracer. Testing covers external visual inspection, dimensional checks, acetone testing, electrical and memory testing, X-ray analysis, and decapsulation. The company reports millions of parts in stock and a 48-hour turnaround from receipt through mitigation to shipment.

Direct Components serves commercial, industrial, and defense/aerospace customers, drawing on a global network of vetted suppliers and 27 years of relationships. Its authorized manufacturer lines include Xilinx/AMD, Analog Devices, Intel, Samsung, Texas Instruments, NXP, Infineon, Vishay, and On Semiconductor, among others. The distributor supplies integrated circuits, memory, microprocessors, transistors, resistors, relays, and other board-level components.

The company emphasizes counterfeit mitigation as a core differentiator, holding AS6081:2012 certification alongside ISO 9001:2015 and AS9120:2016. Its five-pillar control plan covers prevention, risk mitigation, detection, disposition, and training, with GIDEP cross-checks on every lot. A 60-day fit/form/function warranty applies to standard orders, extended to one year for AS6081-certified shipments.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9120:2016','ANSI/ESD S20.20','AS6081:2012']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Independent electronic component distribution", "Obsolete and end-of-life parts sourcing", "Hard-to-find component sourcing", "Excess inventory direct purchase", "Excess inventory consignment", "Excess inventory brokered sales", "In-house quality inspection", "Counterfeit detection and mitigation", "External visual inspection", "Dimensional inspection", "Acetone testing (device surface)", "Electrical testing", "Programming and memory testing", "X-ray inspection", "Decapsulation and internal analysis", "Solderability testing", "Mechanical scrape testing", "GIDEP cross-checks", "Supplier approval and vetting", "Supply chain traceability", "Climate-controlled storage", "ESD packaging and dry packing", "Vacuum sealing", "Certificate of Conformance issuance"], "industries": ["OEMs", "Contract manufacturers (CMs)", "EMS companies", "Electronic component distributors", "Commercial electronics", "Industrial electronics", "Defense and aerospace"], "materials": ["Integrated circuits", "Semiconductors", "Memory devices", "Microprocessors", "Transistors", "Resistors", "Relays"], "equipment": ["Keyence VHX Digital Microscope", "Creative Electron Truview Prime X-Ray", "Hitachi XMET 8000", "Mantis Elite Microscope", "Tektronix 576 Curve Tracer"], "volume": "Millions of in-house parts", "lead_time": "48 hours from receipt through mitigation to shipment", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["48-hour turnaround from part receipt through mitigation testing to shipment", "