ilities) and /about (Since 2014...)", "60-day standard warranty, 1-year on AS6081 orders -> /capabilities (Warranty & Support)", "Serves OEMs, CMs, EMS companies, distributors worldwide -> /about (Our Story)", "Commercial, industrial, defense/aerospace clients -> /about (Our Story)", "Manufacturer lines: Xilinx/AMD, Analog Devices, Altera, Dallas/Maxim, Linear Tech, Intel, Samsung, Cypress, Fairchild, Hitachi, Infineon, Vishay, Motorola, On Semi, NXP/Freescale, National Semi, Texas Instruments -> /about (Our Story)", "Component types: integrated circuits, semiconductors, memory, microprocessors, transistors, resistors, relays -> /about (Our Story)", "Excess inventory programs: direct buy, consignment, brokered -> /services (Surplus Inventory Management) and /capabilities (Transforming Your Inventory...)", "Five-pillar counterfeit control plan -> /capabilities (Our Five Pillar Counterfeit Control Plan)", "Customer portal for order monitoring -> /capabilities (Customer Portal)"], "company_type": null, "makes_products": null, "type_evidence": null, "founded_year": null, "employee_count": null, "cage_code": null, "min_order": null, "export_compliance": null, "languages": null, "social_links": null, "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='direct-components' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in 1970 in Lenexa, Kansas, Disposable Instrument Co has specialized in medical device component manufacturing for over five decades. The company operates as a U.S.-based producer of custom stainless steel surgical components.

The company manufactures a range of precision surgical components including wound drainage trocars, fixation pins, Steinmann pins, K-wires, tunnelers, guide pins, obturators, and handles, points, and ends. All parts are made from surgical- or implant-grade stainless steel certified to ASTM F-899/ISO 7153-1 or ASTM F-138/ISO 5832-1. Disposable Instrument employs proprietary manufacturing processes that yield a distinctive high-gloss finish, and maintains full traceability by part, heat, job, or lot number with records retained for at least seven years. To date, the company has produced over 35 million metal medical device components.

Disposable Instrument serves the medical device industry exclusively, supplying component manufacturers and original equipment manufacturers that require precision stainless steel parts for surgical applications. Its customer base includes firms needing custom trocars, fixation pins, and other implantable or single-use instruments.

The company emphasizes quicker turnaround through inventory management and stocking programs that support multiple release orders, with the ability to work overtime for urgent orders. Manufacturing and customer service are located in the United States, supplemented by European representation. Raw material certification, statistical dimension control, and a focus on reliability are cited as core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','RoHS','REACH','Conflict Minerals Compliance']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom stainless steel surgical component manufacturing", "Proprietary high-gloss finishing", "Material certification and traceability (ASTM F-899, ISO 7153-1, ASTM F-138, ISO 5832-1)", "Statistical process control", "100% visual inspection", "Inventory management and stocking programs", "Quick-turn and urgent order fulfillment", "Design consultation for material alloy selection"], "industries": ["Medical device"], "materials": ["Surgical-grade stainless steel", "Implant-grade stainless steel", "Stainless steel (ASTM F-899, ISO 7153-1, ASTM F-138, ISO 5832-1)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary manufacturing processes yielding high-gloss finish on stainless steel components", "Full traceability by part, heat, job, or lot number with records retained seven-plus years", "Inventory management enabling quicker turnaround and stock for multiple release orders", "U.S.-based manufacturing and customer service with European representation", "Raw material certified to ASTM F-899/ISO 7153-1 and ASTM F-138/ISO 5832-1"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1970 -> /about", "Headquarters Lenexa, Kansas -> db", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /about", "Produced over 35 million metal medical device components -> /about", "Manufactures wound drainage trocars, fixation pins, Steinmann pins, K-wires, tunnelers, guide pins, obturators, handles/points/ends -> /", "Uses surgical-grade and implant-grade stainless s